WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.657 --> 00:00:36.317
Hey, boy! Hey!

2
00:00:36.397 --> 00:00:37.777
Hey, boy!

3
00:01:04.657 --> 00:01:05.797
Hey!

4
00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:25.817
But the only thing that's got to
find her is a great big drink of gin.

5
00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:28.197
Get along there, doggie.

6
00:01:28.497 --> 00:01:30.717
Boy, Lulu tells the sea.

7
00:01:30.797 --> 00:01:33.737
You see, she wears a big white hat.

8
00:01:33.817 --> 00:01:38.957
And I'll bet your life when I'm in
town, the dudes all hit the flat.

9
00:01:39.797 --> 00:01:41.597
Come along, money horse.

10
00:01:56.877 --> 00:02:00.171
Well, here we are in Nebraska,
and I'm telling you, boy,

11
00:02:02.257 --> 00:02:05.797
Me for a can of them Greengate slums.

12
00:02:07.337 --> 00:02:10.957
Well, I tell you what I'm going to do,
I'm going over to Jim's place and get a

13
00:02:11.037 --> 00:02:13.717
quarter of that best scrapper juice of his

14
00:02:14.077 --> 00:02:18.117
and get off in a corner and kind
of slowly strangle it to death.

15
00:02:33.257 --> 00:02:35.357
Do-do-do-do, hurry up there.

16
00:02:45.517 --> 00:02:46.577
Well,

17
00:02:47.337 --> 00:02:49.497
I'll be gall-darned.

18
00:02:52.657 --> 00:02:57.437
Well, Steve, you honor your
low-down son of a bull beaver.

19
00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:00.457
Well, you gall-dang,
nasty, superb buzzard.

20
00:03:00.537 --> 00:03:02.713
What the sandhill are you doing here?

21
00:03:03.257 --> 00:03:06.377
Special well come on
inside I can listen to lies.

22
00:03:06.457 --> 00:03:09.928
You're gonna tell me much
better than a drink under my belt

23
00:03:18.757 --> 00:03:19.777
I

24
00:03:26.737 --> 00:03:31.997
Hey, I heard about your being a
foreman get me laughing for most of week

25
00:03:33.257 --> 00:03:34.577
What have you been doing?

26
00:03:34.657 --> 00:03:37.257
Oh, you know. You know, Count Weasel.

27
00:03:37.337 --> 00:03:39.437
You're just the same as always.

28
00:03:39.517 --> 00:03:40.977
Ain't no accounts for nobody.

29
00:03:41.057 --> 00:03:42.517
Nowhere. That's so.

30
00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.057
Well, I've been having my fun.

31
00:03:44.137 --> 00:03:46.497
I ain't been wasting my
time working like you.

32
00:03:46.577 --> 00:03:47.237
Yeah.

33
00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:48.317
Well,

34
00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:50.437
I'll... Here's my...

35
00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:55.337
Well, I'll be it.

36
00:03:55.417 --> 00:03:56.937
I'm full, I think.

37
00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:02.137
Let's see. It's been about four years
since we burned up the border down in Texas.

38
00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:05.197
Yeah, that's right. Ain't
you ever gonna settle down?

39
00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:05.997
Me?

40
00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:08.617
Put your laughing. Why should I?

41
00:04:12.177 --> 00:04:13.617
I can't expect you.

42
00:04:13.697 --> 00:04:15.097
It's the last roundup.

43
00:04:15.497 --> 00:04:18.321
How about working for me
over at the Buck State?

44
00:04:19.077 --> 00:04:20.637
Maybe I will.

45
00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:22.577
For a while.

46
00:04:30.617 --> 00:04:32.417
I'll bet you five.

47
00:04:33.297 --> 00:04:38.477
Well Steve, I reckon I gotta
learn you all over again.

48
00:04:38.637 --> 00:04:39.997
That's a bet.

49
00:04:43.597 --> 00:04:47.717
Pardon, ma'am. Did I welcome a stranger
to these parts with a shot of liquor?

50
00:04:47.797 --> 00:04:49.017
Si, senor.

51
00:04:49.097 --> 00:04:50.657
Look out for this hombre, ma'am.

52
00:04:50.737 --> 00:04:53.977
He don't mean nothing he
says and he's flat-throat.

53
00:04:54.057 --> 00:04:56.697
Oh, senor, that's too bad, no?

54
00:04:57.017 --> 00:05:01.297
And you? I can toast you in rye
or bourbon till the sun goes down.

55
00:05:01.417 --> 00:05:02.797
Should we start now?

56
00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:06.357
Lowdown buzzard, Joe. Stand off, cow ham.

57
00:05:06.437 --> 00:05:08.037
This lady drinks with me.

58
00:05:08.117 --> 00:05:10.117
Two rye and one bourbon, Joe.

59
00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.477
Hello, Travis.

60
00:05:19.737 --> 00:05:20.897
Hello, Buzz.

61
00:05:21.857 --> 00:05:23.977
Ah, rotten whiskey.

62
00:05:25.097 --> 00:05:26.677
Well, well, well.

63
00:05:26.757 --> 00:05:30.457
Put you boys in line to make some real
money and you throw it away like a lot of

64
00:05:30.537 --> 00:05:32.557
ordinary cow ham.

65
00:05:33.257 --> 00:05:34.437
All right, go ahead.

66
00:05:34.517 --> 00:05:37.817
Go ahead, freeze each other out, and
then I'll sit down and take it away,

67
00:05:37.897 --> 00:05:38.637
brother.

68
00:05:38.717 --> 00:05:40.297
Let's turn on the man.

69
00:05:40.637 --> 00:05:41.637
Them,

70
00:05:43.137 --> 00:05:46.957
and them that don't lord
soften their hard hearts.

71
00:05:48.777 --> 00:05:52.057
I don't know what the argument
is between these two cowhands,

72
00:05:52.137 --> 00:05:56.557
ma'am, but whatever it is, I can
settle a fair square in my favor.

73
00:05:56.637 --> 00:05:58.657
Howdy, champus. When'd you blow in?

74
00:05:58.737 --> 00:05:59.837
Hello, Steve.

75
00:06:00.137 --> 00:06:03.057
Just blowed in to beat
your time with this lady.

76
00:06:03.537 --> 00:06:05.137
Isn't that so, ma'am?

77
00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:08.317
But, senor, I promised to
drink with these gentlemen.

78
00:06:08.397 --> 00:06:08.937
Yeah?

79
00:06:09.017 --> 00:06:11.537
Well, you and me are leaving, see?

80
00:06:11.617 --> 00:06:13.677
Just one minute, please.

81
00:06:13.877 --> 00:06:16.397
Don't look like you're beating
anybody's time, Tramper.

82
00:06:16.477 --> 00:06:17.857
Not even yours.

83
00:06:17.937 --> 00:06:19.557
I ain't arguing with you, sweetheart.

84
00:06:19.637 --> 00:06:20.757
I'm telling you.

85
00:06:22.157 --> 00:06:23.497
There's no argument, Mr.

86
00:06:23.577 --> 00:06:24.377
Tramper.

87
00:06:24.457 --> 00:06:26.557
We're getting along just fine.

88
00:06:26.837 --> 00:06:29.013
Not that it's any of yours, isn't it?

89
00:06:33.257 --> 00:06:34.777
Who's talking to you?

90
00:06:35.977 --> 00:06:37.917
I'm talking to you, Francis.

91
00:06:38.517 --> 00:06:40.737
If I want to know anything
from you, I'll tell you.

92
00:06:40.817 --> 00:06:43.377
You long-legged son of a...

93
00:06:44.397 --> 00:06:46.677
If you want to call me that...

94
00:06:47.037 --> 00:06:48.057
Smile.

95
00:06:54.397 --> 00:06:58.017
With a gun against my belly, I...

96
00:06:58.097 --> 00:07:00.417
I always smile.

97
00:07:15.797 --> 00:07:18.157
You're lucky, Trompas.

98
00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:20.637
That guy is a good shot.

99
00:07:20.717 --> 00:07:24.397
He keeps the metal cans
jumping down the road.

100
00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:26.037
That's it, Pedro.

101
00:07:26.117 --> 00:07:31.757
Well, I know a fellow that can hit three
whiskey glasses in the air at the same

102
00:07:31.837 --> 00:07:32.877
time.

103
00:07:36.817 --> 00:07:39.597
Come on, boys. Get down,
I'll quit my hide off here.

104
00:07:39.677 --> 00:07:40.937
That game is stuck.

105
00:07:41.297 --> 00:07:42.297
Oh.

106
00:07:43.037 --> 00:07:44.137
Hey, boss.

107
00:07:44.337 --> 00:07:46.737
Number three, change it to the
station on account of them cattle,

108
00:07:46.817 --> 00:07:48.477
blocking the whole right-of-way.

109
00:07:48.557 --> 00:07:50.217
All right, I'll tend to that.

110
00:07:50.297 --> 00:07:52.497
I reckon I better dangle
on down there, Steve.

111
00:07:52.577 --> 00:07:53.737
Want to come along?

112
00:07:54.277 --> 00:07:56.277
Sure, I'll help you clean them up.

113
00:08:09.797 --> 00:08:10.917
Hey, listen to you.

114
00:08:10.997 --> 00:08:15.056
You blow that whistle again, and
I'll blow you right out of that cab.

115
00:08:18.917 --> 00:08:20.977
Hey, old sheepherder, how'd you like that?

116
00:08:21.057 --> 00:08:22.697
Don't you call me, old sheepherder?

117
00:08:22.777 --> 00:08:24.937
You grizzled old walrus, you!

118
00:08:25.017 --> 00:08:27.057
What's that? There, I told you.

119
00:08:27.877 --> 00:08:29.297
Keep your shirt on, partner.

120
00:08:29.377 --> 00:08:31.897
These cows just hang around
your engine to keep warm.

121
00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:33.297
Well, listen, get them off.

122
00:08:33.377 --> 00:08:35.937
I've done my stretch, and I
want to go home and go to bed.

123
00:08:36.017 --> 00:08:38.429
You better get your head back in that cab

124
00:08:40.897 --> 00:08:41.897
Steve,

125
00:08:42.197 --> 00:08:45.897
you go down there with me and bring the
rest of that bunch back and I'll set a hold

126
00:08:45.977 --> 00:08:47.177
to it. Jack!

127
00:08:47.897 --> 00:08:51.257
Tina, popcorn, candy and chewing wax.

128
00:08:51.337 --> 00:08:54.937
All kinds of cigars,
cigarettes and tobacco.

129
00:08:55.017 --> 00:08:57.135
We'll be in the station in a minute.

130
00:08:57.557 --> 00:08:59.677
My goodness, this is terrible.

131
00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:02.577
I never saw so many wild cows in my life.

132
00:09:02.657 --> 00:09:04.177
It's much like Vermont, is it?

133
00:09:04.257 --> 00:09:05.657
I should say not.

134
00:09:11.637 --> 00:09:12.957
Howdy, ma'am.

135
00:09:13.097 --> 00:09:14.957
Getting off at Medicine Bowl?

136
00:09:15.217 --> 00:09:16.217
Yes.

137
00:09:16.557 --> 00:09:18.397
Since we never get there.

138
00:09:18.737 --> 00:09:21.577
Say, you ain't the new waitress
for the Lone Star Hotel,

139
00:09:21.657 --> 00:09:22.477
are you?

140
00:09:22.557 --> 00:09:24.857
No, I'm snoozing you.

141
00:09:24.937 --> 00:09:27.417
Oh, the new school farm for St.C.

142
00:09:27.497 --> 00:09:28.797
Uh-huh.

143
00:09:30.857 --> 00:09:33.237
I wasn't expecting anybody to meet me.

144
00:09:33.317 --> 00:09:37.017
Well, ma'am, we wasn't expecting
to meet you, but here we are,

145
00:09:37.097 --> 00:09:39.717
ma'am. Yes, ma'am, here we are.

146
00:09:39.797 --> 00:09:42.617
I've found a different
average kid in Wyoming, too.

147
00:09:42.697 --> 00:09:44.057
Oh, that's fine.

148
00:09:44.537 --> 00:09:46.157
How many told an audience something here?

149
00:09:46.237 --> 00:09:49.177
Quite about 19, counting
the Indians in half-read.

150
00:09:49.257 --> 00:09:51.237
He's a lion pole, can't admit.

151
00:09:51.317 --> 00:09:53.677
There ain't but 13 all-toed.

152
00:09:54.097 --> 00:09:56.877
Sam, what you gonna learn then, kid?

153
00:09:56.957 --> 00:09:59.697
Readin' and writin'
and figuring up figures?

154
00:09:59.777 --> 00:10:02.437
Yes, and history and geography.

155
00:10:02.697 --> 00:10:06.257
Oh, yeah. Well, we're so darn good
to know somethin' about geography.

156
00:10:06.337 --> 00:10:09.808
They ain't got a liquor sense
about knowin' where we're at.

157
00:10:25.537 --> 00:10:26.877
Thank you so much.

158
00:10:26.957 --> 00:10:28.957
And now where do we find the safe?

159
00:10:30.417 --> 00:10:31.977
Follow me, ma'am.

160
00:10:32.157 --> 00:10:34.337
And you'll never go astray.

161
00:10:34.857 --> 00:10:36.317
Right this way.

162
00:10:49.577 --> 00:10:52.317
Hey, ma'am, that sitter
won't hurt you none.

163
00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:14.497
I think it's safe now, ma'am.

164
00:11:15.557 --> 00:11:16.717
Thank you.

165
00:11:16.797 --> 00:11:19.097
Molly, lucky thing I happened alone.

166
00:11:19.177 --> 00:11:22.457
A wild steer is an awful, ornery critter.

167
00:11:22.717 --> 00:11:24.517
Oh, it did frighten me.

168
00:11:24.597 --> 00:11:26.077
Just for a moment.

169
00:11:26.257 --> 00:11:29.257
That's it. Seeing you face to
face like I'm doing now, ma'am.

170
00:11:29.337 --> 00:11:30.897
You couldn't have been to me.

171
00:11:30.977 --> 00:11:32.257
Oh, thank you.

172
00:11:32.337 --> 00:11:35.157
I'm glad my man got your
bags all right, ma'am.

173
00:11:36.277 --> 00:11:38.517
Take the lady's things right
over the stagecoach, will you,

174
00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:39.597
Steven?

175
00:11:41.717 --> 00:11:42.917
Oh, boy.

176
00:11:43.097 --> 00:11:44.097
Oh.

177
00:11:46.417 --> 00:11:47.477
Come on.

178
00:11:49.157 --> 00:11:53.451
Here, Ella, you better take your moo
cow home or your mom will spank you.

179
00:11:54.337 --> 00:11:55.237
Yes.

180
00:11:55.317 --> 00:11:56.517
Come on, Mark.

181
00:12:07.897 --> 00:12:12.457
Perhaps you'd like to rescue that
little girl from that wild deer.

182
00:12:12.537 --> 00:12:16.337
I'm sure she'd be impressed, but
if you tried to make a fool of her,

183
00:12:16.417 --> 00:12:18.237
she'd probably slap your face.

184
00:12:18.497 --> 00:12:21.717
I'm really obliged to you,
sir, for helping me.

185
00:12:21.797 --> 00:12:23.503
It's a great pleasure, ma'am.

186
00:12:24.857 --> 00:12:26.537
That'll be all, my man.

187
00:12:29.337 --> 00:12:30.517
Here you are.

188
00:12:33.277 --> 00:12:35.237
Why don't you take good
care of this lady, Ben?

189
00:12:35.317 --> 00:12:36.717
She's a special friend of mine.

190
00:12:36.797 --> 00:12:38.197
She's going down to Taylor's.

191
00:12:38.277 --> 00:12:40.097
Sure, I'll take good care of her.

192
00:12:40.177 --> 00:12:42.117
You don't need a friend of this.

193
00:12:47.557 --> 00:12:50.077
Who is that dark man who's so good to me?

194
00:12:50.617 --> 00:12:53.017
Oh, just a mangy foreman, ma'am.

195
00:12:54.117 --> 00:12:55.237
Oh,

196
00:12:55.477 --> 00:12:56.297
goodbye.

197
00:12:56.377 --> 00:12:58.137
Bye. All right, Joe.

198
00:13:06.637 --> 00:13:08.137
Smart, ain't you, Steve?

199
00:13:08.217 --> 00:13:09.457
Smart pal.

200
00:13:09.817 --> 00:13:14.797
In case you got any ideas about my new
lady friend, I just want to warn you that

201
00:13:14.877 --> 00:13:17.417
school moms ain't in your class.

202
00:13:17.557 --> 00:13:19.897
Oh, you're warning me.

203
00:13:19.977 --> 00:13:21.137
Mm-hmm.

204
00:13:21.337 --> 00:13:22.877
Well, Steve,

205
00:13:23.097 --> 00:13:25.797
usually I just beat you by nose.

206
00:13:26.137 --> 00:13:28.617
This time I'm going to
throw you in hog tight.

207
00:13:28.697 --> 00:13:30.297
Oh, you don't tell me.

208
00:13:30.377 --> 00:13:31.377
Mm-hmm.

209
00:13:37.757 --> 00:13:39.357
Stop this thing now.

210
00:13:39.437 --> 00:13:41.877
You stop this wagon now.

211
00:13:45.697 --> 00:13:48.317
Put them boots on, Pa, Huey.

212
00:13:48.397 --> 00:13:51.117
Oh, Ma, they're too
tight across the street.

213
00:13:51.777 --> 00:13:53.737
Miss Taylor won't mind these suppos.

214
00:13:53.817 --> 00:13:55.577
You will put them on.

215
00:13:56.037 --> 00:13:59.157
Land sakes, look at all them folks there.

216
00:13:59.237 --> 00:14:02.857
Well, you think they was welcoming the
president of the United States instead of a

217
00:14:02.937 --> 00:14:03.937
school marm?

218
00:14:04.017 --> 00:14:06.237
If I ever get them on,
I'll have to cut them off.

219
00:14:06.317 --> 00:14:07.737
You put them on.

220
00:14:08.137 --> 00:14:09.137
Susan,

221
00:14:09.517 --> 00:14:13.377
take your fingers out of them sausages, or
you'll get a bellyache and your mar will

222
00:14:13.457 --> 00:14:15.657
blame me. I don't care.

223
00:14:15.737 --> 00:14:17.437
Put them both on now.

224
00:14:24.397 --> 00:14:25.937
I'm coming right over.

225
00:14:26.017 --> 00:14:27.357
All right.

226
00:14:29.357 --> 00:14:30.877
Well, Uncle Huey.

227
00:14:30.957 --> 00:14:33.017
Hello, Dad. How are you? How are you?

228
00:14:33.097 --> 00:14:35.817
Good to see you. We've run the twist.

229
00:14:35.897 --> 00:14:39.577
Rode 40 miles and still as dry as a bone.

230
00:14:39.657 --> 00:14:41.257
You're very lucky, Mrs.

231
00:14:41.337 --> 00:14:43.537
Huey. Very lucky.

232
00:14:45.217 --> 00:14:48.197
Alex, you put your cabs
to pass in the bedroom.

233
00:14:48.277 --> 00:14:50.557
They can get a little
nap before the Christmas.

234
00:14:50.637 --> 00:14:52.537
I'll be here until later.

235
00:14:52.617 --> 00:14:54.457
Miss Taylor, Miss Taylor.
What's the matter, Hans?

236
00:14:54.537 --> 00:14:56.057
You come here, pick.

237
00:14:56.137 --> 00:14:59.117
Excuse me, Pope Hans got his
help all snarled up about.

238
00:14:59.197 --> 00:15:00.517
I'll run along.

239
00:15:00.677 --> 00:15:02.377
Well, now, what's the trouble, Hans?

240
00:15:02.457 --> 00:15:03.997
Look at them picking.

241
00:15:05.437 --> 00:15:06.757
Oh, you picking.

242
00:15:07.517 --> 00:15:09.357
Well, if it's a saint, Emily.

243
00:15:09.997 --> 00:15:11.557
Try to hatch them apples.

244
00:15:11.637 --> 00:15:13.237
Always wantin' to be a mother, ain't you?

245
00:15:13.317 --> 00:15:14.997
If you only knew, Emily.

246
00:15:15.077 --> 00:15:15.897
Now, get.

247
00:15:15.977 --> 00:15:16.977
Get.

248
00:15:17.377 --> 00:15:19.495
Well, now, Hans, what's the trouble?

249
00:15:20.637 --> 00:15:23.177
I can't do anything.

250
00:15:23.277 --> 00:15:25.877
All right, I'll take some place, brother.

251
00:15:27.117 --> 00:15:29.477
Buggy, hurry up with
them chickens and ducks.

252
00:15:29.557 --> 00:15:32.457
Keep that flan-eyed musk right
away and we'll get through.

253
00:15:32.537 --> 00:15:34.337
Go on, chink. Chop your soy.

254
00:15:34.417 --> 00:15:35.737
Miss Della, Miss Della.

255
00:15:35.817 --> 00:15:37.197
We got no milk.

256
00:15:37.277 --> 00:15:38.117
Why not?

257
00:15:38.197 --> 00:15:39.737
Cowboy, no jazim.

258
00:15:46.317 --> 00:15:49.717
Why, you yellow-bellied biscuits!

259
00:15:52.637 --> 00:15:55.077
Sam, it's awful cold in here.

260
00:15:55.157 --> 00:15:57.137
Give me that Coke, Boleg.

261
00:15:58.397 --> 00:16:01.737
Why, Sam, your whole
body's changing color.

262
00:16:01.997 --> 00:16:03.717
Hurry up, you wondering, Paulcat.

263
00:16:03.797 --> 00:16:04.797
Yes, ma'am.

264
00:16:04.997 --> 00:16:07.397
Boleg, hurry up and get out of that tower.

265
00:16:07.477 --> 00:16:10.037
You're cleaning up. I need you out here.

266
00:16:10.117 --> 00:16:11.677
Just keep your shirt on, Mr.

267
00:16:11.757 --> 00:16:12.757
Taylor.

268
00:16:13.077 --> 00:16:14.997
Now, don't you know I was in here?

269
00:16:15.077 --> 00:16:17.197
That woman knows everything.

270
00:16:17.577 --> 00:16:19.457
Here she is now, folk.

271
00:16:20.637 --> 00:16:23.117
Why, it's just grand having you here.

272
00:16:23.197 --> 00:16:28.417
Folks, this is Miss Molly Wood, the new
school mom, all the way from Vermont.

273
00:16:31.277 --> 00:16:33.957
What are them cow curds up to now?

274
00:16:39.637 --> 00:16:41.497
You look here now, honey, we can do it.

275
00:16:41.577 --> 00:16:42.517
You quit making that noise.

276
00:16:42.597 --> 00:16:43.917
You'll wake up them babies.

277
00:16:43.997 --> 00:16:46.497
Stop trying to shoot them cans open.

278
00:16:46.757 --> 00:16:49.017
Here, use this cleaver.

279
00:16:49.537 --> 00:16:52.877
All right, Miss Taylor,
but it'll take a heap longer.

280
00:16:53.777 --> 00:16:55.217
Hello, boys.

281
00:16:57.017 --> 00:16:58.017
Howdy,

282
00:16:58.637 --> 00:17:00.990
boys. Getting ready for the celebration?

283
00:17:01.537 --> 00:17:02.857
Howdy, Travis.

284
00:17:03.557 --> 00:17:06.717
You got here just too
late to work, didn't you?

285
00:17:07.017 --> 00:17:11.297
In the cool of the evening, when the
food and liquor and women is ready.

286
00:17:11.497 --> 00:17:13.277
That's when I appear.

287
00:17:13.737 --> 00:17:15.637
I see. Hello, honey.

288
00:17:15.977 --> 00:17:17.506
Where's the liquor barrel?

289
00:17:22.177 --> 00:17:23.497
What do you say, boy?

290
00:17:23.577 --> 00:17:24.577
It's Steve.

291
00:17:25.157 --> 00:17:28.417
What are you trailing
around with the trampers for?

292
00:17:29.357 --> 00:17:31.837
Why are you fellas all sore at tramping?

293
00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:33.357
He's all right.

294
00:17:34.257 --> 00:17:35.757
Yes, he is.

295
00:17:35.837 --> 00:17:37.657
In a big belief.

296
00:17:39.997 --> 00:17:42.397
You looking for someone, Miss Ward?

297
00:17:42.537 --> 00:17:44.857
Oh, no, I get interested
in seeing everybody.

298
00:17:44.937 --> 00:17:47.057
It's all so new to me. Oh.

299
00:17:47.677 --> 00:17:49.497
Are all the cowboys here now?

300
00:17:49.577 --> 00:17:51.277
Sure, I hope so.

301
00:17:52.177 --> 00:17:53.877
I've never been invited.

302
00:17:54.717 --> 00:17:57.057
A whole lot of them, Miss Bella.

303
00:17:57.137 --> 00:17:58.237
You know this lady.

304
00:17:58.317 --> 00:18:00.757
Can I go ring a bell? All I have.

305
00:18:01.597 --> 00:18:04.357
Dinner, everybody, come and get it.

306
00:18:04.437 --> 00:18:07.057
Come on, Miss Porter. Won't
you just sit ahead of the table?

307
00:18:07.137 --> 00:18:08.137
Come on.

308
00:18:08.757 --> 00:18:10.597
Come and get it.

309
00:18:13.417 --> 00:18:16.657
Now you, children. Come on,
now you get out of that place.

310
00:18:16.737 --> 00:18:18.757
Come on, come on.

311
00:18:34.637 --> 00:18:35.637
Come on!

312
00:18:38.777 --> 00:18:41.237
Ghosty ladies, just you know!

313
00:18:50.397 --> 00:18:52.977
The Valley Ratchets have
another meeting today.

314
00:18:53.057 --> 00:18:55.437
And they're fighting for giving up.

315
00:18:55.577 --> 00:18:57.677
I can tell you that the
country is the devil.

316
00:18:57.757 --> 00:19:00.657
That pays a man better
to steal than to work.

317
00:19:00.737 --> 00:19:03.917
I think it's getting close
to his showdown, Judge.

318
00:19:04.737 --> 00:19:06.617
That's her standing in the window now.

319
00:19:06.697 --> 00:19:08.657
Careful, Russell has got to stop.

320
00:19:08.737 --> 00:19:11.097
Yeah, ain't she pretty, though?

321
00:19:11.557 --> 00:19:13.439
I wonder if she can dance to it.

322
00:19:14.297 --> 00:19:15.977
Are you listening to me?

323
00:19:16.577 --> 00:19:17.737
Sure, Judge.

324
00:19:17.977 --> 00:19:19.577
And I agree with you.

325
00:19:20.037 --> 00:19:21.357
My throat's mighty dusty.

326
00:19:21.437 --> 00:19:22.397
Let's go in the house.

327
00:19:22.477 --> 00:19:24.457
I think we can find
something in the house, maybe.

328
00:19:24.537 --> 00:19:25.737
I hope so. Sure, that...

329
00:19:25.817 --> 00:19:27.817
That ain't no way for a fella
like you to make a living,

330
00:19:27.897 --> 00:19:28.397
Steve.

331
00:19:28.317 --> 00:19:31.737
Don't I know it? Cow hands
is dumber than a local steer.

332
00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:34.557
Freeze all winter, bake all summer.

333
00:19:34.637 --> 00:19:35.557
For what?

334
00:19:35.637 --> 00:19:39.317
For just to get enough money
to get drunk 12 times a year.

335
00:19:39.397 --> 00:19:42.221
Yeah, but money's easy
when you're smart, Steve.

336
00:19:42.417 --> 00:19:45.857
But you'll never get it
balloping cows for $30 a month.

337
00:19:49.237 --> 00:19:51.777
Why didn't you wait for
me, Steve, this evening?

338
00:19:51.857 --> 00:19:56.217
Oh, you was late and Trampas
dangled by, so I came along with him.

339
00:19:56.297 --> 00:19:58.709
You ain't very cheesy about your company.

340
00:19:59.257 --> 00:20:01.157
Maybe you'll explain
what you mean by that.

341
00:20:01.237 --> 00:20:02.897
Nothing, Trampas. Nothing.

342
00:20:02.977 --> 00:20:05.677
Maybe I could tell you a belly
full and maybe I couldn't.

343
00:20:05.757 --> 00:20:06.897
What are you driving at?

344
00:20:06.977 --> 00:20:09.257
Maybe I ought to compliment you, Trampas.

345
00:20:09.337 --> 00:20:12.697
You've got so many calves this
year, your cows must have litter.

346
00:20:12.777 --> 00:20:13.977
Like a sow.

347
00:20:14.057 --> 00:20:16.897
Reckoning it keeps you
all wore out branding them.

348
00:20:16.977 --> 00:20:19.897
You're liable to talk yourself
into a heap of trouble, my friend.

349
00:20:19.977 --> 00:20:22.417
Since when was I your friend, Trampas?

350
00:20:22.817 --> 00:20:24.737
Oh, all right.

351
00:20:25.657 --> 00:20:27.097
That suits me.

352
00:20:28.477 --> 00:20:31.183
How about circulating
around the dance, Steve?

353
00:20:40.997 --> 00:20:43.337
Why don't you let him say that to you?

354
00:20:43.717 --> 00:20:45.317
Because I'm smart.

355
00:20:46.017 --> 00:20:47.957
One job at a time.

356
00:20:48.737 --> 00:20:50.537
Never lose your temper.

357
00:20:53.737 --> 00:20:57.117
There she is. She looks pretty
in her Vermont fashion dress,

358
00:20:57.197 --> 00:20:57.837
don't you?

359
00:20:57.917 --> 00:21:00.777
She looks good in an
Indian squall blanket.

360
00:21:01.237 --> 00:21:03.717
I know I got the inside track with her.

361
00:21:03.797 --> 00:21:05.857
I want to give you an even break.

362
00:21:06.117 --> 00:21:08.477
I'll meet you to see who
asked her for the first dance.

363
00:21:08.557 --> 00:21:09.557
This.

364
00:21:10.057 --> 00:21:11.857
You son of a gun, you.

365
00:21:11.937 --> 00:21:13.337
How do you know?

366
00:21:14.857 --> 00:21:19.897
Is it true, Miss, that France is going to
give us that Statue of Liberty that she's

367
00:21:19.977 --> 00:21:21.317
been talking about?

368
00:21:23.017 --> 00:21:25.937
Oh, yes. It was in the
paper just before I left.

369
00:21:26.877 --> 00:21:29.097
Excuse me, please. Yes, surely.

370
00:21:33.917 --> 00:21:35.517
Good evening, ma'am.

371
00:21:36.137 --> 00:21:38.697
Would you care to try a turn at Dancin's?

372
00:21:40.117 --> 00:21:42.517
You're from Virginia, I understand.

373
00:21:42.917 --> 00:21:44.037
Yes, ma'am.

374
00:21:44.117 --> 00:21:45.997
That is, I was born there.

375
00:21:46.437 --> 00:21:49.877
I always thought the Southerners
had such good manners.

376
00:21:52.057 --> 00:21:53.697
That's correct, ma'am.

377
00:21:53.817 --> 00:21:56.237
Leastways they should have.

378
00:21:56.317 --> 00:21:58.837
Well, in New England, where I came from,

379
00:22:00.277 --> 00:22:03.757
Ask to be introduced to a lady
before he asks her to dance.

380
00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:07.837
I ask your pardon, ma'am.

381
00:22:09.217 --> 00:22:10.517
Pardon me, ma'am.

382
00:22:11.057 --> 00:22:14.377
I see you didn't dance
with that big galoo.

383
00:22:14.457 --> 00:22:18.037
Can't blame you, none. There ain't any
of the girls want to dance with him.

384
00:22:18.117 --> 00:22:20.177
Would you like to spin around with me?

385
00:22:20.257 --> 00:22:23.669
I kind of figured we were
introduced by that stage driver.

386
00:22:24.417 --> 00:22:26.477
Why, yes, I love you.

387
00:22:41.517 --> 00:22:44.517
I guess Eastern dancing
is kind of different, huh?

388
00:22:44.597 --> 00:22:46.417
I'm sorry I'm so awkward.

389
00:22:46.537 --> 00:22:48.037
Oh, that's all right, ma'am.

390
00:22:48.117 --> 00:22:49.997
You'll pick it up in no time.

391
00:22:52.597 --> 00:22:57.857
Say, Judge, I wonder if you'd
oblige me in a little social matter.

392
00:22:57.937 --> 00:22:59.097
What is it?

393
00:23:00.677 --> 00:23:03.417
I'd like you to introduce
me to the new school mom.

394
00:23:03.497 --> 00:23:05.117
Uh, formal like.

395
00:23:05.197 --> 00:23:07.777
But from all the talking you've done about
her, I thought you and her are pretty

396
00:23:07.857 --> 00:23:08.857
good friends.

397
00:23:09.357 --> 00:23:11.945
Didn't I see you talking
to her a while ago?

398
00:23:12.577 --> 00:23:13.877
Who? Me?

399
00:23:15.357 --> 00:23:18.886
I don't know what you're up to,
young fella, but I'll do it.

400
00:23:23.037 --> 00:23:24.277
Thank you, man.

401
00:23:24.357 --> 00:23:25.537
The honor is all mine.

402
00:23:25.617 --> 00:23:29.323
Excuse me, Miss Wood, but this
young man says he never met you.

403
00:23:30.457 --> 00:23:31.637
I... Well, that is...

404
00:23:31.717 --> 00:23:35.246
Well, you all know. He's been
talking about you for a month.

405
00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:39.197
Allow me to make you a claim of Miss Wood.

406
00:23:39.277 --> 00:23:40.557
Thanks, me too.

407
00:23:41.297 --> 00:23:45.417
Oh, you're the gallant young man
that rescued me from a tame cow.

408
00:23:45.917 --> 00:23:47.677
Oh, I'm sorry, ma'am.

409
00:23:48.597 --> 00:23:52.244
I'm sorry, ma'am, but you must
admit this is a genuine rescue.

410
00:23:52.357 --> 00:23:56.457
And you must excuse my friend, Steve,
for being so clumsy and bold-legged.

411
00:23:56.537 --> 00:23:58.137
Would you care to sit down?

412
00:23:58.457 --> 00:24:01.197
Well, thank you. I am a little tired.

413
00:24:01.297 --> 00:24:03.277
I'd rather talk and dance.

414
00:24:03.357 --> 00:24:07.063
Well, I can't talk and dance
very well at the same time anyhow.

415
00:24:07.377 --> 00:24:09.277
So sit down by the window.

416
00:24:17.977 --> 00:24:21.117
We sure are glad to have
you out here, Miss Wood.

417
00:24:21.997 --> 00:24:23.177
Thank you.

418
00:24:23.957 --> 00:24:27.137
Now that we've been formally introduced...

419
00:24:27.637 --> 00:24:30.757
I'd like very much to go
riding with you someday.

420
00:24:31.377 --> 00:24:32.557
Oh, yes?

421
00:24:36.697 --> 00:24:38.557
You ain't afraid of me, are you, ma'am?

422
00:24:38.637 --> 00:24:39.977
Why should I be?

423
00:24:40.597 --> 00:24:42.157
No reason so.

424
00:24:42.417 --> 00:24:44.497
I'm as gentle as a plow horse.

425
00:24:44.977 --> 00:24:47.517
And I'm powerful interested in education.

426
00:24:47.917 --> 00:24:50.446
Then I hope you come
to some of my classes.

427
00:24:50.677 --> 00:24:53.657
I have several little boys, just your age.

428
00:24:55.317 --> 00:24:58.037
Does the book learn to
do a cow hand any good?

429
00:24:59.937 --> 00:25:03.172
Oh, it won't be all reading
and writing and arithmetic.

430
00:25:03.857 --> 00:25:07.117
I hope to teach my
children good manners, too.

431
00:25:07.777 --> 00:25:09.797
I'm sorry, ma'am, but...

432
00:25:09.877 --> 00:25:11.217
if you thought I...

433
00:25:11.297 --> 00:25:14.437
if you thought I aimed
to treat you that way...

434
00:25:14.517 --> 00:25:16.797
you see, out here...

435
00:25:17.157 --> 00:25:19.937
us folks... we don't exactly under...

436
00:25:20.017 --> 00:25:22.997
well, you see, you're...
you're from the east...

437
00:25:23.817 --> 00:25:27.517
We've been out here so long and
the outdoors is kind of wild.

438
00:25:27.717 --> 00:25:29.677
Well, I tell you, when I first...

439
00:25:29.757 --> 00:25:31.177
When I first...

440
00:25:31.257 --> 00:25:33.077
I can't realize I was here with you.

441
00:25:33.157 --> 00:25:35.177
Miss Molly, the person's here.

442
00:25:35.257 --> 00:25:36.904
Won't you come and meet him?

443
00:25:38.837 --> 00:25:40.297
Dr. McBride? Yes?

444
00:25:40.377 --> 00:25:42.877
This is Miss Molly Wood,
our new school teacher.

445
00:25:42.957 --> 00:25:44.417
Well, I...

446
00:25:44.497 --> 00:25:45.497
I...

447
00:25:45.717 --> 00:25:48.997
Really, I'm glad to meet you, Miss Wood.

448
00:25:54.077 --> 00:25:57.117
Hey, Steve, where'd you rustle the cake?

449
00:25:59.317 --> 00:26:01.697
Me for them there crullers.

450
00:26:07.417 --> 00:26:09.617
The cake's in the interest to you.

451
00:26:09.697 --> 00:26:13.957
I expect to out inform me that this is
the most elegant lady of this outfit.

452
00:26:14.037 --> 00:26:17.637
She promised me the pleasure
of seeing her home to her cabin.

453
00:26:17.717 --> 00:26:19.157
You don't tell me.

454
00:26:19.257 --> 00:26:21.397
Well, now, ain't that just fine?

455
00:26:22.877 --> 00:26:26.137
Ain't nobody I'd rather
see beat my time than you.

456
00:26:26.217 --> 00:26:29.417
I don't trust you no more
than a half-bleed bandit.

457
00:26:29.677 --> 00:26:31.217
This fish is a speckle trap.

458
00:26:31.297 --> 00:26:34.037
You are? I guess you better
leave that door open, Mr.

459
00:26:34.117 --> 00:26:35.677
Stark. It's kind of stuffy in there.

460
00:26:35.757 --> 00:26:37.217
All right, I reckon they won't wake up.

461
00:26:37.297 --> 00:26:38.617
Now, boys, be careful.

462
00:26:38.697 --> 00:26:41.109
Don't make no noise. You'll wake them up.

463
00:26:41.797 --> 00:26:44.091
But they got corralled in there anyhow.

464
00:26:51.277 --> 00:26:52.737
Babies, aren't they?

465
00:26:53.217 --> 00:26:55.737
Never saw so many mavericks in my life.

466
00:26:56.877 --> 00:26:58.297
Them's the kids.

467
00:26:58.817 --> 00:27:01.405
And some of them's
waiting to be christened.

468
00:27:02.437 --> 00:27:08.777
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven,

469
00:27:08.857 --> 00:27:13.817
eight, nine, ten, eleven,
beautiful sleeping angels.

470
00:27:14.997 --> 00:27:16.057
Say,

471
00:27:16.317 --> 00:27:19.457
it'd be funny if they got mixed up
and some of them was christened wrong,

472
00:27:19.537 --> 00:27:20.537
wouldn't it?

473
00:27:21.117 --> 00:27:24.077
A yon-reload down horse, these you.

474
00:27:24.557 --> 00:27:26.357
Oh, he says be funny.

475
00:27:35.837 --> 00:27:38.697
Get busy before the parson goes to work.

476
00:27:42.817 --> 00:27:45.137
This must be that Jasper brat.

477
00:27:45.937 --> 00:27:47.937
Looks like he has a itch.

478
00:27:51.237 --> 00:27:54.708
I wonder what these little
byrons think about all day long.

479
00:27:55.137 --> 00:27:57.417
Not a god darn thing.

480
00:28:10.897 --> 00:28:13.557
Getting mighty swampy around this bed.

481
00:28:16.577 --> 00:28:20.077
Oh, well, this is up to
change our whole life.

482
00:28:22.577 --> 00:28:24.517
Look out, look out.

483
00:28:24.997 --> 00:28:27.457
Now keep peace with you, little maverick.

484
00:28:34.137 --> 00:28:36.077
Stop playing now, boys.

485
00:28:36.557 --> 00:28:38.637
Listen, folks, it's getting late.

486
00:28:38.717 --> 00:28:41.797
Some of you women have got to
drive all night to get home.

487
00:28:41.877 --> 00:28:44.157
So let's christen the babies now.

488
00:28:45.977 --> 00:28:48.917
This country sure is getting fancy.

489
00:28:49.097 --> 00:28:50.677
Christening babies.

490
00:28:51.117 --> 00:28:56.117
important school more pretty soon
they'll be putting soda pop in the liquor

491
00:28:56.197 --> 00:29:00.977
that's when i'll be
getting out me too just

492
00:29:01.057 --> 00:29:06.557
right in here folks if you want to see
the ceremony here's the christening water

493
00:29:06.637 --> 00:29:13.037
fountain it's publicly clean been boiled
and strange for a new sock fine the

494
00:29:13.117 --> 00:29:14.197
child please

495
00:29:16.337 --> 00:29:18.997
Name the child. Charles Augustus.

496
00:29:19.077 --> 00:29:20.077
Jeffrey.

497
00:29:20.277 --> 00:29:22.957
Charles Augustus. I christened him...

498
00:29:23.037 --> 00:29:24.017
Oh, wait a minute.

499
00:29:24.097 --> 00:29:25.757
Why, that ain't Charles Augustus.

500
00:29:25.837 --> 00:29:27.957
That's one of Uncle Huey's wrath.

501
00:29:28.937 --> 00:29:29.937
What?

502
00:29:30.297 --> 00:29:31.297
Here.

503
00:29:31.477 --> 00:29:34.237
Oh, come to your fall, lay your night.

504
00:29:34.317 --> 00:29:36.877
No, not the real night.
This is Charles Augustus.

505
00:29:36.957 --> 00:29:38.337
Charles Augustus is nothing.

506
00:29:38.417 --> 00:29:39.817
But I've just christened him.

507
00:29:39.897 --> 00:29:40.937
Then you'll unchristen him.

508
00:29:41.017 --> 00:29:44.577
Oh, it can't be done. You unchristen this
child or you don't get another nickel out

509
00:29:44.657 --> 00:29:45.657
of me.

510
00:29:46.797 --> 00:29:48.457
Both! Both! Both!

511
00:29:48.537 --> 00:29:53.617
Something terrible! Someone has mixed
these kids and we can't tell which is what!

512
00:29:53.697 --> 00:29:54.697
Oh, boy!

513
00:29:55.857 --> 00:29:57.477
Have you got a photo?

514
00:29:57.857 --> 00:30:00.357
Uh, let me... You've got a photo.

515
00:30:01.797 --> 00:30:04.697
There's my daughter and I've been
afraid to come down this year...

516
00:30:04.777 --> 00:30:06.697
...is someone I've never seen before!

517
00:30:06.777 --> 00:30:08.117
Oh, there's mine!

518
00:30:08.377 --> 00:30:09.637
There's your hand!

519
00:30:09.717 --> 00:30:10.917
You're going in, my sister!

520
00:30:10.997 --> 00:30:14.173
I'm mine! I'm not going to
tell you what you're doing!

521
00:30:17.837 --> 00:30:19.697
I don't know!

522
00:30:34.197 --> 00:30:36.097
Something's got to be done about that.

523
00:30:36.177 --> 00:30:39.517
The most distressing and
reprehensible occurrence.

524
00:30:39.597 --> 00:30:40.637
Reprehensible?

525
00:30:40.717 --> 00:30:43.597
It's Mangy. I call it plain Mangy.

526
00:30:43.677 --> 00:30:46.197
Dickens would say if
they found out it was us.

527
00:30:46.277 --> 00:30:48.957
Some honorary Polk has done this delivery.

528
00:30:49.037 --> 00:30:52.657
Well, who was it? Let's find the credit
that did it, I'll brand him plenty.

529
00:30:52.737 --> 00:30:54.557
He oughta been strung up.

530
00:30:54.917 --> 00:30:56.437
Yeah, don't worry, Steve.

531
00:30:56.577 --> 00:30:58.477
They ain't gonna find out we done it.

532
00:30:58.557 --> 00:31:01.097
Listen, we ain't left no clue.

533
00:31:06.157 --> 00:31:07.977
The fun's all over.

534
00:31:08.077 --> 00:31:11.357
I'm gonna be moseying out
before something does happen.

535
00:31:13.137 --> 00:31:15.457
Hey, what's that on Steve's pants?

536
00:31:16.797 --> 00:31:18.257
For the land of the land!

537
00:31:18.337 --> 00:31:19.757
For that bad cat!

538
00:31:19.837 --> 00:31:22.517
Where is the poor cat? Go get him!

539
00:31:35.357 --> 00:31:38.557
I'm sorry, ma'am, about
what happened to Steve.

540
00:31:38.837 --> 00:31:40.717
But now Steve's gone.

541
00:31:41.317 --> 00:31:42.757
Could I see your home?

542
00:31:42.837 --> 00:31:44.997
I saw you pin that cap on Steve.

543
00:31:46.597 --> 00:31:48.957
treating those poor babies that way?

544
00:31:49.037 --> 00:31:54.257
Well, you see, I heard that some of them
was female, so I had them introduced all

545
00:31:54.337 --> 00:31:55.157
around.

546
00:31:55.237 --> 00:31:57.397
I think your conduct is disgraceful.

547
00:31:57.477 --> 00:31:59.197
Yes, ma'am. No, ma'am.

548
00:31:59.277 --> 00:32:02.937
I suppose you're proud of yourself, playing
a trick like that on those poor mothers?

549
00:32:03.017 --> 00:32:03.877
No, ma'am.

550
00:32:03.957 --> 00:32:04.597
Yes.

551
00:32:04.677 --> 00:32:07.457
I suppose you call yourself
a grown-up responsible man.

552
00:32:07.537 --> 00:32:08.237
Yes.

553
00:32:08.317 --> 00:32:09.597
Yes. No, ma'am.

554
00:32:09.677 --> 00:32:11.457
Well, you asked if you were a child.

555
00:32:11.537 --> 00:32:12.037
Yes.

556
00:32:12.097 --> 00:32:13.277
No, ma'am.

557
00:32:13.377 --> 00:32:15.906
Is that all you've got
to say for yourself?

558
00:32:17.017 --> 00:32:19.137
I don't think you're a bit funny.

559
00:32:26.717 --> 00:32:28.157
Now that's the right piece.

560
00:32:28.237 --> 00:32:30.297
You were way off key last time.

561
00:32:31.077 --> 00:32:32.497
Now all together.

562
00:32:41.237 --> 00:32:42.417
You're the one that's wrong.

563
00:32:42.497 --> 00:32:44.321
Now let's hear you by yourself.

564
00:32:48.377 --> 00:32:49.617
All right.

565
00:32:49.697 --> 00:32:50.697
And you?

566
00:32:54.557 --> 00:32:55.837
That's better.

567
00:32:56.057 --> 00:32:59.528
All together now. And don't
forget where your line came in.

568
00:33:46.537 --> 00:33:48.897
Oh, my God.

569
00:34:19.817 --> 00:34:22.157
I told you I'd go riding
with you after school.

570
00:34:22.237 --> 00:34:25.766
Well, I was just helping you
so you get it finished quicker.

571
00:34:32.697 --> 00:34:35.697
I'm afraid that herd of
yours is about to stampede.

572
00:34:36.037 --> 00:34:38.508
Sounds like it. I'll go see what I can do.

573
00:34:46.537 --> 00:34:47.277
That's enough.

574
00:34:47.357 --> 00:34:48.957
Wine, wine.

575
00:34:49.037 --> 00:34:51.077
Green, wine, wine.

576
00:34:51.157 --> 00:34:52.157
That's enough.

577
00:34:56.757 --> 00:34:59.937
Children, on account of Splendid,
where you learned that song,

578
00:35:00.017 --> 00:35:03.782
I'm going to let you go 10 minutes
early, so school's dismissed.

579
00:35:10.817 --> 00:35:13.177
I've got a little surprise for you today.

580
00:35:13.257 --> 00:35:14.277
What is it?

581
00:35:14.717 --> 00:35:16.597
Oh, a new horse.

582
00:35:18.197 --> 00:35:21.317
Is it gentle? Yes, I broke myself.

583
00:35:21.397 --> 00:35:24.637
And he gave me more trouble
than you had, gentle than me.

584
00:35:24.717 --> 00:35:26.117
I'll change my writing habit.

585
00:35:26.197 --> 00:35:27.077
I won't be in just a minute.

586
00:35:27.157 --> 00:35:27.897
Don't go.

587
00:35:27.977 --> 00:35:30.697
Do me a favor and go just as you are.

588
00:35:30.777 --> 00:35:34.797
I'm sure the host won't mind, and
I like you so much in that dress.

589
00:35:35.997 --> 00:35:37.057
All right.

590
00:35:42.677 --> 00:35:43.837
Thank you.

591
00:35:46.097 --> 00:35:47.357
What's her name?

592
00:35:48.897 --> 00:35:51.017
What are you laughing about now?

593
00:35:51.337 --> 00:35:52.337
Well,

594
00:35:52.737 --> 00:35:55.855
her name is Sir Henry, but
I call him Hank, for sure.

595
00:36:07.277 --> 00:36:09.917
You haven't told me about
that book I lent you last week.

596
00:36:09.997 --> 00:36:11.237
Did you finish it?

597
00:36:11.337 --> 00:36:13.137
That Romeo and Juliet?

598
00:36:13.557 --> 00:36:15.557
Yes, ma'am. I'll finish it.

599
00:36:15.737 --> 00:36:17.797
Don't tell me you didn't like it.

600
00:36:20.097 --> 00:36:22.937
Well, I haven't read any poetry before.

601
00:36:23.457 --> 00:36:26.477
As soon as I get the hang of it, it'll
be as easy as reading the Patent Madison

602
00:36:26.557 --> 00:36:27.557
catalog.

603
00:36:28.157 --> 00:36:30.039
Well, didn't you like the story?

604
00:36:30.677 --> 00:36:33.597
Well, they raised a mighty
strange breed of men in them days.

605
00:36:33.677 --> 00:36:36.417
But in some respects, this
Romeo was a pretty good hombre.

606
00:36:36.497 --> 00:36:39.197
Oh, indeed. Just a pretty good hombre.

607
00:36:39.497 --> 00:36:41.577
Yes, he had his enemies and killed them.

608
00:36:41.657 --> 00:36:44.737
He was no coward and was a good one.

609
00:36:45.137 --> 00:36:47.317
Do you approve of killing your enemies?

610
00:36:47.397 --> 00:36:50.817
No. I don't know if he
was an honorable way out.

611
00:36:50.897 --> 00:36:51.657
No matter.

612
00:36:51.737 --> 00:36:53.957
But those enemies were very ornery.

613
00:36:54.037 --> 00:36:55.677
They had it coming to him.

614
00:36:55.877 --> 00:36:58.577
What else? What did you like about Romeo?

615
00:36:58.837 --> 00:37:01.397
I didn't like him in that balcony scene.

616
00:37:01.617 --> 00:37:03.157
The balcony scene?

617
00:37:03.397 --> 00:37:05.557
That's the most famous scene in the play.

618
00:37:05.637 --> 00:37:07.597
Maybe so, but not for me.

619
00:37:08.697 --> 00:37:10.537
He was snipping down that rope ladder.

620
00:37:10.617 --> 00:37:12.377
Why did he not talk to us?

621
00:37:12.457 --> 00:37:14.857
Why did he not go in
through the front door?

622
00:37:14.937 --> 00:37:16.437
Do you understand?

623
00:37:16.517 --> 00:37:18.297
Their families were enemies.

624
00:37:18.377 --> 00:37:19.377
Exactly.

625
00:37:20.817 --> 00:37:23.297
That's not my idea of a real man.

626
00:37:23.557 --> 00:37:24.877
What would you do?

627
00:37:24.957 --> 00:37:26.597
Go in and kill a father?

628
00:37:26.677 --> 00:37:28.017
That would be nice.

629
00:37:28.097 --> 00:37:29.637
No, I would not have killed him.

630
00:37:29.717 --> 00:37:32.217
But I would have had a
showdown with him, man to man.

631
00:37:32.297 --> 00:37:36.177
If he was too stubborn to call off that
fool feud, I would have grabbed Juliet right

632
00:37:36.257 --> 00:37:38.577
off that balcony and married her.

633
00:37:38.697 --> 00:37:40.017
What did he do?

634
00:37:41.297 --> 00:37:42.797
What did he do?

635
00:37:44.877 --> 00:37:46.297
He loved Juliet.

636
00:37:46.377 --> 00:37:48.377
He fell in love with him.

637
00:37:48.457 --> 00:37:50.217
Why did he get to go?

638
00:37:51.077 --> 00:37:55.717
In those days, I realized how
much women loved the gallantry.

639
00:37:56.317 --> 00:37:57.817
Yes, I know.

640
00:37:57.937 --> 00:38:01.037
He couldn't resist playing
an actor on that balcony.

641
00:38:01.117 --> 00:38:03.757
He wasted so much time
and got them both killed.

642
00:38:03.837 --> 00:38:05.377
If I loved a girl,

643
00:38:05.757 --> 00:38:09.097
and wanted her, I knew
I could take care of her.

644
00:38:09.697 --> 00:38:13.757
Not in the words of Romeo,
but in the feelings inside.

645
00:38:13.957 --> 00:38:15.997
Do you think I'd let that
gulf stand between us?

646
00:38:16.077 --> 00:38:18.917
Pritt around on rope
ladders, making up poetry?

647
00:38:19.097 --> 00:38:21.297
No, you're hardly a Romeo.

648
00:38:21.377 --> 00:38:22.797
But what would you do?

649
00:38:27.317 --> 00:38:29.637
Molly, I'll show you what I'd do.

650
00:38:38.617 --> 00:38:41.676
You're just as sure of
yourself as ever, aren't you?

651
00:38:42.557 --> 00:38:44.737
Molly, don't play with me.

652
00:38:45.017 --> 00:38:46.797
We don't fool each other.

653
00:38:47.517 --> 00:38:49.477
We ain't on no balcony.

654
00:38:49.737 --> 00:38:53.037
Don't you think the spring is the
prettiest time of year to be married?

655
00:38:53.117 --> 00:38:55.337
But I don't want to get married yet.

656
00:38:55.897 --> 00:39:00.097
I've got my school, and I'm just getting
started, and no children can get into

657
00:39:00.177 --> 00:39:00.997
school.

658
00:39:01.077 --> 00:39:03.237
That ain't no real woman's job in life.

659
00:39:03.317 --> 00:39:04.577
Listen, Molly.

660
00:39:05.437 --> 00:39:07.477
I don't want to stay here.

661
00:39:08.177 --> 00:39:11.057
Not if you'll be my wife and partner.

662
00:39:11.137 --> 00:39:12.777
And what I want to do...

663
00:39:13.257 --> 00:39:16.597
I'm pushing out further
west to Utah or Nevada.

664
00:39:17.017 --> 00:39:20.097
To do what Judge Henry
did right here in Wyoming.

665
00:39:20.177 --> 00:39:23.517
To make more United States
out of raw prairie land.

666
00:39:24.977 --> 00:39:26.557
I like you.

667
00:39:26.757 --> 00:39:29.757
And I admire you more than
any man I've ever known.

668
00:39:30.397 --> 00:39:32.857
But I'm not sure of myself yet.

669
00:39:34.077 --> 00:39:36.317
He's so new and strange.

670
00:39:36.757 --> 00:39:38.717
I feel like an alien.

671
00:39:39.617 --> 00:39:41.077
An outsider.

672
00:39:41.357 --> 00:39:45.757
I don't know how to explain it,
but I just feel that I'm different.

673
00:39:46.837 --> 00:39:48.537
Women are funny, Molly.

674
00:39:48.957 --> 00:39:50.937
I don't understand them.

675
00:39:51.077 --> 00:39:52.237
Oh, yes, you do.

676
00:39:52.317 --> 00:39:54.137
But I'm glad you think you do.

677
00:39:58.237 --> 00:39:59.537
What is it?

678
00:40:01.017 --> 00:40:03.037
Sounds like a cat woman.

679
00:40:05.217 --> 00:40:06.217
Arrrr!

680
00:40:12.537 --> 00:40:14.197
Find out what the trouble is.

681
00:40:14.277 --> 00:40:15.317
All right.

682
00:40:17.157 --> 00:40:18.857
Come on, Lordy, horse.

683
00:40:24.217 --> 00:40:25.537
I'll be right back.

684
00:41:02.797 --> 00:41:05.497
Thank you.

685
00:41:44.257 --> 00:41:45.497
Hello, Steve.

686
00:41:45.577 --> 00:41:48.812
I didn't know you were coming
up this end of the range.

687
00:41:49.457 --> 00:41:51.357
Oh, I'm just kind of...

688
00:41:51.677 --> 00:41:53.397
kind of drifting around.

689
00:41:54.797 --> 00:41:58.237
I've just been putting a
monogram on a couple of strays.

690
00:42:00.377 --> 00:42:02.617
Yes, so I noticed.

691
00:42:05.097 --> 00:42:06.117
Steve.

692
00:42:07.197 --> 00:42:09.417
There's no use talking around things.

693
00:42:09.497 --> 00:42:12.977
You've been putting Travis's
brand on somebody else's calf.

694
00:42:14.257 --> 00:42:18.357
Oh, what's a few calves more or
less to a man that's got thousands?

695
00:42:18.857 --> 00:42:23.257
I'm sick of a nursemaid in someone else's
cows around for no more than enough to

696
00:42:23.337 --> 00:42:24.984
keep you in smoking tobacco.

697
00:42:25.197 --> 00:42:27.137
Don't talk that away, Steve.

698
00:42:28.397 --> 00:42:31.037
You and I have done a lot
of local things together.

699
00:42:31.117 --> 00:42:35.117
But there are some things that
ain't only local, they're plum wrong.

700
00:42:35.377 --> 00:42:37.917
Ah, you take life too seriously.

701
00:42:39.217 --> 00:42:42.177
This whole country's taking
things more seriously.

702
00:42:42.397 --> 00:42:44.317
I ain't trying to lecture you.

703
00:42:44.397 --> 00:42:47.077
I play Sunday on what's right or wrong.

704
00:42:47.757 --> 00:42:51.577
The ranchers are getting plums thick
of having their herds trimmed out.

705
00:42:51.657 --> 00:42:55.128
And there'll soon be posses
out with ropes on their saddle.

706
00:42:55.297 --> 00:42:57.137
Times are changing, Steve.

707
00:42:57.417 --> 00:43:00.711
They can't get away with this
sort of thing much longer.

708
00:43:00.917 --> 00:43:01.937
Well,

709
00:43:02.357 --> 00:43:06.057
I'm carrying a nice limber
rope to make it easy for them.

710
00:43:06.477 --> 00:43:08.717
If they catch me.

711
00:43:10.357 --> 00:43:12.917
To blame hard-headed fool you.

712
00:43:13.397 --> 00:43:14.817
What are you going to do?

713
00:43:14.897 --> 00:43:16.317
Turn me in?

714
00:43:16.797 --> 00:43:17.817
Steve,

715
00:43:18.817 --> 00:43:20.657
nobody's talking about that.

716
00:43:21.717 --> 00:43:25.188
I reckon I couldn't be sore
at you, no matter what you did.

717
00:43:26.537 --> 00:43:28.177
But listen, Steve.

718
00:43:28.817 --> 00:43:34.177
You and I have been friends too long to
find ourselves lined up on opposite sides in

719
00:43:34.257 --> 00:43:35.597
anything like this.

720
00:43:36.357 --> 00:43:38.697
Don't put me in any hole like that.

721
00:43:38.937 --> 00:43:40.597
Oh, shucks.

722
00:43:40.897 --> 00:43:43.317
How do I know what I'm gonna do?

723
00:43:44.097 --> 00:43:46.697
This country's getting too civilized.

724
00:43:46.777 --> 00:43:48.237
Too solemn.

725
00:43:48.997 --> 00:43:52.237
I got a notion I'll be moseying out.

726
00:43:52.777 --> 00:43:54.977
The goldfield is somewhere.

727
00:43:56.137 --> 00:43:58.297
There's no need to leave him, Steve.

728
00:43:58.697 --> 00:44:01.797
You know you can stay on
here as long as you want.

729
00:44:02.337 --> 00:44:03.917
Yeah, I know.

730
00:44:04.537 --> 00:44:06.897
The mingy old buzzard.

731
00:44:41.377 --> 00:44:43.537
Well, there they go, Steve.

732
00:44:43.757 --> 00:44:45.337
Right on time.

733
00:44:58.637 --> 00:45:03.397
The only thing I don't like about this
stealing business is the hard work.

734
00:45:05.837 --> 00:45:07.857
Hard work, but easy picking.

735
00:45:13.157 --> 00:45:15.510
You've got it all straight, haven't you?

736
00:45:15.757 --> 00:45:19.437
Let at least a hundred head of the soren
craters stay on the bank and leave them

737
00:45:19.517 --> 00:45:20.517
there.

738
00:45:21.037 --> 00:45:24.757
So in case anybody's trailing us, they'll
think we got scared and left the whole

739
00:45:24.837 --> 00:45:25.837
bunch.

740
00:45:26.737 --> 00:45:28.917
You swim the rest down the river.

741
00:45:29.297 --> 00:45:33.117
And don't let a hoof touch the shore
until they hit the rocks at Boulder Creek.

742
00:45:33.197 --> 00:45:35.021
Or they won't leave any tracks.

743
00:45:35.357 --> 00:45:36.237
Savvy?

744
00:45:36.317 --> 00:45:37.517
All right.

745
00:45:37.637 --> 00:45:39.877
But I think you're crazy
for leaving any of them.

746
00:45:39.957 --> 00:45:40.957
Yeah.

747
00:45:42.217 --> 00:45:44.657
You gotta pay, you gotta pay
a little for safety, you know,

748
00:45:44.737 --> 00:45:45.417
Steve.

749
00:45:45.497 --> 00:45:47.937
Throw away one, grab two.

750
00:45:48.797 --> 00:45:50.697
Always play percentages.

751
00:45:51.017 --> 00:45:52.717
Never try to be a hog.

752
00:45:53.517 --> 00:45:54.797
Percentages, Steve.

753
00:45:55.537 --> 00:45:57.497
I learned that dealing Pharaoh.

754
00:45:58.397 --> 00:45:59.617
Remember that.

755
00:45:59.957 --> 00:46:01.817
All right, Trampitt. Go ahead.

756
00:46:01.897 --> 00:46:02.937
Come on, boy.

757
00:46:05.997 --> 00:46:07.457
Atta, Huckleberry.

758
00:46:45.957 --> 00:46:47.917
Hey, Baldi!

759
00:46:47.997 --> 00:46:48.997
Baldi!

760
00:47:01.857 --> 00:47:03.577
Baldi! Baldi!

761
00:47:11.297 --> 00:47:12.397
We got a pretty good bunch.

762
00:47:12.477 --> 00:47:15.077
I don't think we'd find
hide a hair of them.

763
00:47:15.937 --> 00:47:16.937
Well,

764
00:47:17.337 --> 00:47:18.717
locate any more, Nebraska?

765
00:47:18.797 --> 00:47:21.077
Most a hundred heads so far.

766
00:47:21.817 --> 00:47:24.757
Say, this country's just
full of stolen cattle.

767
00:47:24.837 --> 00:47:27.077
And they ain't a cow thief in sight.

768
00:47:27.157 --> 00:47:30.216
Looks like they got leery
and dumped the whole herd.

769
00:47:30.557 --> 00:47:32.677
Yeah, and they'll get them
bum out of the country.

770
00:47:32.757 --> 00:47:34.897
We never will know just who they are.

771
00:47:34.977 --> 00:47:37.477
A plaza couldn't find
them in them blind canyon.

772
00:47:37.557 --> 00:47:38.677
They were all dead a week.

773
00:47:38.757 --> 00:47:40.557
I reckon we'll lick, boys.

774
00:47:40.637 --> 00:47:42.497
Lucky to get our cattle back.

775
00:47:42.657 --> 00:47:47.217
Yeah, you found all your cattle but
about 200 head of your best beef.

776
00:47:47.517 --> 00:47:50.317
What do you mean? We'll
never get the rest of them?

777
00:47:50.397 --> 00:47:52.977
You notice they found nothing but scrubs.

778
00:47:53.297 --> 00:47:55.097
They must have went someplace.

779
00:47:55.177 --> 00:47:57.197
Them cows can't fly.

780
00:47:57.597 --> 00:48:00.757
And they're doing good
thing they can't to die.

781
00:48:02.557 --> 00:48:05.577
Boys, we're playing out in the water.

782
00:48:05.757 --> 00:48:08.117
They swim them cows downstream.

783
00:48:08.757 --> 00:48:10.217
Do anything you want to bet.

784
00:48:10.297 --> 00:48:13.377
We'll pick up them tracks
the other side of Lavagat.

785
00:48:13.917 --> 00:48:16.037
Probably Boulder Creek, huh?

786
00:48:16.377 --> 00:48:17.917
Through the rocks, sure.

787
00:48:18.017 --> 00:48:20.517
They picked a tough route to Jackson Hole.

788
00:48:20.597 --> 00:48:22.477
We'll be able to run with them
smelling this and something,

789
00:48:22.557 --> 00:48:24.257
but poor at nightfall.

790
00:48:24.337 --> 00:48:26.677
I'll pick up the rest of the
bunch and we'll get started.

791
00:48:26.757 --> 00:48:28.816
By gosh, boy, I believe he's right.

792
00:48:29.277 --> 00:48:30.937
And you can bet he's right.

793
00:48:31.017 --> 00:48:35.977
And what's more, the guy that's bossing
this spread ain't no common cow seed.

794
00:48:36.217 --> 00:48:38.957
He's cuter than a mountain
goat in springtime.

795
00:48:39.037 --> 00:48:41.837
He ain't no smarter
than that, Virginia boys.

796
00:48:42.437 --> 00:48:43.337
Yep.

797
00:48:43.417 --> 00:48:47.777
Say that boy is so smart,
he dries snow and sells it for sugar.

798
00:48:49.417 --> 00:48:51.257
Come on boys, let's run for a horse.

799
00:48:51.337 --> 00:48:54.737
Well, I'll leave a couple of boys
around cattle down here with them.

800
00:48:54.817 --> 00:48:56.582
Okay, Fred, let's go. Come on.

801
00:49:11.877 --> 00:49:14.337
Not bad for a three days' work.

802
00:49:14.577 --> 00:49:17.437
200 head worth more than 75 a piece.

803
00:49:17.897 --> 00:49:19.677
Better than a herd and
cow's for a living, isn't it?

804
00:49:19.757 --> 00:49:21.937
Damn, still, where do
you think we are now?

805
00:49:22.017 --> 00:49:23.977
In some swell New York hotel?

806
00:49:24.057 --> 00:49:27.257
Oh, we soon will be along
about two months from now.

807
00:49:29.477 --> 00:49:31.637
Hey, Trampon, what's that fire be?

808
00:49:31.717 --> 00:49:32.677
What do you think we want to do?

809
00:49:32.757 --> 00:49:33.697
Let somebody know we're here?

810
00:49:33.777 --> 00:49:34.637
Hey, listen.

811
00:49:34.717 --> 00:49:36.897
When I want a fire, I ain't gonna have it.

812
00:49:36.977 --> 00:49:39.657
If there's anybody following us, they're
40 miles back, cooling their heels.

813
00:49:39.737 --> 00:49:42.857
Yeah, hunting cow tracks under the water.

814
00:49:44.417 --> 00:49:47.757
Well, I'm going to dangle down the ravine
and see how greasy is getting along night

815
00:49:47.837 --> 00:49:49.137
herding them critters.

816
00:49:54.717 --> 00:49:57.482
What's the matter, Jim?
Anything bothering you?

817
00:49:57.817 --> 00:50:00.217
What? It's all right for Trampas to talk.

818
00:50:00.297 --> 00:50:02.677
I'll be glad when we get rid of them cows.

819
00:50:02.757 --> 00:50:04.517
What if they do catch you?

820
00:50:04.597 --> 00:50:06.957
You can only die one time.

821
00:50:07.037 --> 00:50:08.877
Sure, what do you want?

822
00:50:09.737 --> 00:50:11.777
Yeah, what's life anyway?

823
00:50:11.857 --> 00:50:15.677
A few winters waiting for spring,
a few summers wishing they'd last,

824
00:50:15.757 --> 00:50:19.377
a few bottles of whiskey and a
half a dozen girls you can remember.

825
00:50:19.457 --> 00:50:22.597
And then your little six by
three feet under the ground,

826
00:50:22.677 --> 00:50:24.517
and that's all.

827
00:50:25.037 --> 00:50:27.597
Might as well be now as later.

828
00:50:39.737 --> 00:50:41.477
Be greedy, baby. Sit down.

829
00:50:41.657 --> 00:50:43.897
I'll send one of the other
boys over to help you.

830
00:50:43.977 --> 00:50:45.097
All right.

831
00:50:45.837 --> 00:50:46.957
Hey, look!

832
00:50:56.857 --> 00:50:58.457
Looks like a pasture.

833
00:50:59.257 --> 00:51:00.517
We'd better duck and warn them.

834
00:51:00.597 --> 00:51:01.837
Oh, nothing. I'm drifting.

835
00:51:01.917 --> 00:51:03.858
You go your way and I'll go mine.

836
00:51:14.037 --> 00:51:16.097
You know that he found him.

837
00:51:16.177 --> 00:51:17.797
What's biting him anyway?

838
00:51:17.877 --> 00:51:20.995
I don't know, but he's sure
bothered about something.

839
00:51:25.697 --> 00:51:28.477
Boys, we're gonna split
into three parties.

840
00:51:28.557 --> 00:51:29.910
We'll close in on them.

841
00:51:30.677 --> 00:51:33.324
Foster, you take your
boys down by the creek.

842
00:51:33.557 --> 00:51:35.397
You boys come with me.

843
00:51:39.557 --> 00:51:41.417
Besides, the moon's too bright.

844
00:51:41.497 --> 00:51:42.837
I don't like that either.

845
00:51:42.917 --> 00:51:45.997
If they couldn't get us by sunlight,
they're not going to buy moonlight,

846
00:51:46.077 --> 00:51:46.577
Jim.

847
00:51:46.577 --> 00:51:47.217
Yeah.

848
00:51:47.297 --> 00:51:49.617
Well, I wish I was in
Jackson Hole right now.

849
00:51:49.697 --> 00:51:53.657
Say, for God's sake, can't you
get that bird off your face?

850
00:51:53.757 --> 00:51:55.337
Think of something cheerful.

851
00:51:55.417 --> 00:51:57.577
Your girl or a cold bottle of beer.

852
00:51:57.657 --> 00:51:59.277
Sure, sure.

853
00:51:59.817 --> 00:52:02.517
Hey, play on that tune I learned you.

854
00:52:02.597 --> 00:52:03.597
You know.

855
00:52:11.737 --> 00:52:14.477
Oh, my God, what do you say?

856
00:52:14.697 --> 00:52:17.357
They don't know how to kiss you.

857
00:52:17.437 --> 00:52:20.977
And the sound of the sound of the sound...

858
00:52:21.057 --> 00:52:24.277
With the to-do-do-do-do-do-do...

859
00:52:24.357 --> 00:52:27.177
With the to-do-do-do-do...

860
00:52:27.257 --> 00:52:30.597
They don't know how to kiss you.

861
00:52:33.477 --> 00:52:35.457
Take it, boys!

862
00:52:41.737 --> 00:52:43.297
Get their guns, honey.

863
00:52:43.557 --> 00:52:44.997
How are you?

864
00:52:45.157 --> 00:52:48.277
Boys, where is your calling card?

865
00:52:48.357 --> 00:52:50.517
Get in there. Never mind,
we left them in the deck.

866
00:52:50.597 --> 00:52:52.657
Thanks for the ditty, Pedro.

867
00:52:52.737 --> 00:52:54.537
It's real entertaining.

868
00:52:54.617 --> 00:52:56.197
I want to do something like this.

869
00:52:56.277 --> 00:52:57.997
Where's Trampas and the rest?

870
00:52:58.077 --> 00:52:59.157
Trampas?

871
00:53:00.437 --> 00:53:03.277
You got us all wrong, partner.

872
00:53:03.357 --> 00:53:07.377
Only us three out on
a little hunting trip.

873
00:53:07.457 --> 00:53:08.437
Yeah.

874
00:53:08.517 --> 00:53:12.437
You must have been drinking your
coffee with a cup in each hand.

875
00:53:25.717 --> 00:53:27.277
Time, boys.

876
00:53:28.437 --> 00:53:30.597
I'm going to take a look around.

877
00:53:35.857 --> 00:53:37.737
I've got another one, boys.

878
00:53:55.977 --> 00:53:57.177
Howdy, boys.

879
00:53:57.257 --> 00:53:59.677
I didn't expect you to find you here.

880
00:54:02.017 --> 00:54:04.377
Whoever was nice heard noon dusk.

881
00:54:07.757 --> 00:54:08.917
I'm up.

882
00:54:09.917 --> 00:54:13.237
Real accommodating of you
boys building this fire for us.

883
00:54:13.317 --> 00:54:15.257
We smelled it right across Wyoming.

884
00:54:15.337 --> 00:54:17.057
I told you I wouldn't
be lighting that fire.

885
00:54:17.137 --> 00:54:17.897
Who who?

886
00:54:17.977 --> 00:54:23.497
You always was a rotten liar, Steve.

887
00:54:23.597 --> 00:54:25.377
You got four of us.

888
00:54:25.517 --> 00:54:27.337
Ain't that enough for one gathering?

889
00:54:27.417 --> 00:54:29.177
Not by a long sight.

890
00:54:34.497 --> 00:54:35.457
No.

891
00:54:35.537 --> 00:54:38.197
We'll take them to the cabin by the hook.

892
00:54:38.497 --> 00:54:40.077
Maybe we'll catch the rest of them.

893
00:54:40.157 --> 00:54:42.457
Come on, boys. I'm out of the back, Annie.

894
00:54:42.537 --> 00:54:44.017
You fellas got the naked.

895
00:54:53.557 --> 00:54:55.137
Well, she's breaking.

896
00:54:55.837 --> 00:54:57.484
Daylight before you know it.

897
00:54:57.737 --> 00:55:00.384
The boys ought to be
showing up any time now.

898
00:55:00.877 --> 00:55:02.995
I didn't look for her until morning.

899
00:55:04.557 --> 00:55:07.217
Hey, when are you going to do this thing?

900
00:55:07.977 --> 00:55:09.317
Turn up, I reckon.

901
00:55:10.737 --> 00:55:12.277
Keep quiet, Jimmy.

902
00:55:14.417 --> 00:55:17.237
We fooled you fellas
good a couple of times.

903
00:55:17.737 --> 00:55:19.557
Thought you'd lost our trail.

904
00:55:20.017 --> 00:55:22.817
You can't beat that
Dublin back in the water.

905
00:55:23.197 --> 00:55:25.597
I learned that trick off in an engine.

906
00:55:26.137 --> 00:55:28.666
Funny how you pick up
this thing, ain't it?

907
00:55:29.417 --> 00:55:32.241
You never know when it's
going to come in handy.

908
00:55:46.457 --> 00:55:49.497
I'll be glad when this is all over with.

909
00:55:49.577 --> 00:55:51.137
It ain't over for me.

910
00:55:51.217 --> 00:55:51.957
Now?

911
00:55:52.037 --> 00:55:53.637
I'm heading for the Teton.

912
00:55:53.717 --> 00:55:54.717
Hunting?

913
00:55:55.057 --> 00:55:56.717
Yeah, hunting.

914
00:55:58.037 --> 00:56:02.737
Ain't only one hombre responsible
for this, and that's Travis.

915
00:56:02.817 --> 00:56:04.877
Enough of that. I'm hunting
Trampers till I find him.

916
00:56:04.957 --> 00:56:06.617
Here's some of the boys now.

917
00:56:08.257 --> 00:56:11.697
We ain't caught hiding our
hair, not any of them both.

918
00:56:12.637 --> 00:56:14.697
I told you to win no more of it.

919
00:56:14.777 --> 00:56:17.130
Come on, let's get this thing over with.

920
00:56:20.397 --> 00:56:24.397
It's a pity to waste that loyalty
on a drunk-legged Trampers.

921
00:56:33.737 --> 00:56:35.657
Come on, boys.

922
00:56:35.937 --> 00:56:37.317
Let's get going.

923
00:56:38.077 --> 00:56:39.257
Come on.

924
00:56:39.337 --> 00:56:40.617
Let's go.

925
00:57:07.417 --> 00:57:08.957
I don't want to die.

926
00:57:09.657 --> 00:57:10.617
Leave it alone.

927
00:57:10.697 --> 00:57:11.797
Take him up a bit.

928
00:57:11.997 --> 00:57:13.937
I don't want to die.

929
00:57:14.297 --> 00:57:15.577
Shut up, Jim.

930
00:57:15.657 --> 00:57:17.457
Take your medicine, Grace.

931
00:57:17.637 --> 00:57:19.417
Why don't you ask him for a drink?

932
00:57:19.497 --> 00:57:21.077
Maybe that will help you.

933
00:57:39.697 --> 00:57:40.697
Nebraska.

934
00:57:44.857 --> 00:57:46.437
You can have this.

935
00:57:48.697 --> 00:57:50.897
Don't worry, I didn't steal it.

936
00:57:50.977 --> 00:57:54.717
Don't forget to wind it and keep the
stem side up and it'll always run.

937
00:57:54.797 --> 00:57:57.797
And it's good for $4
in any regular saloon.

938
00:57:58.537 --> 00:58:00.297
Thank you, Steve.

939
00:58:07.097 --> 00:58:09.237
You can have my saddle, honey.

940
00:58:09.857 --> 00:58:11.397
Thank you, Steve.

941
00:58:13.457 --> 00:58:15.197
That's a good name.

942
00:58:28.637 --> 00:58:30.837
I got the other heart now boys

943
00:58:53.837 --> 00:58:56.017
You got my gun, ain't you, honey?

944
00:58:56.117 --> 00:58:56.797
Yeah.

945
00:58:56.877 --> 00:58:58.177
I want you to keep it with this.

946
00:58:58.257 --> 00:59:00.697
And give it to him.

947
00:59:01.437 --> 00:59:02.917
After it's all over.

948
00:59:05.617 --> 00:59:09.357
I wish it was a tramp,
instead of you, Steve.

949
00:59:14.457 --> 00:59:16.117
I don't want to die.

950
00:59:16.297 --> 00:59:17.877
All right, bring him on, boys.

951
00:59:17.957 --> 00:59:20.277
I don't want to die. No, I'm kidding.

952
00:59:59.457 --> 01:00:01.281
You don't want to say anything.

953
01:00:57.017 --> 01:00:59.637
If he wanted you to have this,

954
01:01:00.997 --> 01:01:03.937
there's a note inside the holster.

955
01:01:34.357 --> 01:01:36.597
It's full of fish this season.

956
01:02:06.537 --> 01:02:08.157
Come on, Marty Wolf.

957
01:02:58.837 --> 01:03:00.037
How is he?

958
01:03:00.117 --> 01:03:01.777
He's still unconscious.

959
01:03:01.857 --> 01:03:03.777
But the doctor says he's out of danger.

960
01:03:03.857 --> 01:03:05.877
You know he belongs in a hospital.

961
01:03:05.957 --> 01:03:07.797
Schoolmarm's house ain't no place for him.

962
01:03:07.877 --> 01:03:09.677
What'd they fetch him here for anyway?

963
01:03:09.757 --> 01:03:12.937
They didn't fetch him.
His horse brung him here.

964
01:03:13.537 --> 01:03:14.777
Funny, ain't it?

965
01:03:14.917 --> 01:03:16.397
No, it ain't funny.

966
01:03:16.477 --> 01:03:18.757
Say, he's been hanging
around here so much.

967
01:03:18.837 --> 01:03:20.737
The horse thought he was home.

968
01:03:24.997 --> 01:03:27.057
Well, here you are at last.

969
01:03:27.737 --> 01:03:29.477
Where did you get that medicine?

970
01:03:29.557 --> 01:03:30.797
In a saloon?

971
01:03:30.917 --> 01:03:34.397
No, I was waiting in there
while the doctor mixed it up.

972
01:03:44.677 --> 01:03:46.957
It's about time you showed up, honey.

973
01:03:47.037 --> 01:03:49.757
If we had to depend on you,
he'd have been dead already.

974
01:03:49.837 --> 01:03:50.837
Yes, ma'am.

975
01:03:51.357 --> 01:03:52.897
Don't go to me, Taylor.

976
01:03:52.977 --> 01:03:54.677
It's a long way to town.

977
01:03:55.837 --> 01:03:59.397
You boys have been just wonderful
coming here and seeing him every day.

978
01:03:59.477 --> 01:04:00.857
That's better for you, Miss Molly.

979
01:04:00.937 --> 01:04:02.297
I reckon we'd have lost him.

980
01:04:02.377 --> 01:04:03.377
Honey,

981
01:04:03.777 --> 01:04:05.537
now you wait outside with the other boys.

982
01:04:05.617 --> 01:04:07.037
I'll be wanting to use you later.

983
01:04:07.117 --> 01:04:08.117
Yes, ma'am.

984
01:04:11.637 --> 01:04:13.537
Now, you quit your worrying, dearie.

985
01:04:13.617 --> 01:04:15.317
He's coming along fine.

986
01:04:15.737 --> 01:04:18.897
Why don't you do what I told you and close
up your school for this afternoon so you

987
01:04:18.977 --> 01:04:20.157
can get some rest?

988
01:04:20.377 --> 01:04:24.097
Now, you've been here every minute
that you ain't teaching them kids.

989
01:04:24.177 --> 01:04:27.937
And you haven't had the right
kind of sleep since he's been sick.

990
01:04:28.017 --> 01:04:29.917
I'm all right. I'm not a bit tired.

991
01:04:29.997 --> 01:04:31.517
I know better.

992
01:04:31.597 --> 01:04:35.537
There ain't nobody can do two jobs
at once without getting tagged out.

993
01:04:35.617 --> 01:04:36.917
Except me.

994
01:04:37.757 --> 01:04:38.777
Nonsense.

995
01:04:39.577 --> 01:04:41.297
Research is over now.

996
01:04:41.517 --> 01:04:42.997
I have to be going back.

997
01:04:50.557 --> 01:04:53.217
Thank you, boys. All right, Miss Molly.

998
01:04:54.177 --> 01:04:56.717
Oh, honey, I meant to ask you,
have you seen Steve around?

999
01:04:56.797 --> 01:04:57.977
Steve, Mom.

1000
01:04:58.737 --> 01:04:59.737
Oh,

1001
01:04:59.817 --> 01:05:00.457
sure.

1002
01:05:00.537 --> 01:05:02.777
Steve ain't with the Box H no more.

1003
01:05:02.857 --> 01:05:05.717
Oh, I thought it was funny
he hadn't been around.

1004
01:05:05.797 --> 01:05:08.097
Well, if you see him,
tell him his gun is here.

1005
01:05:08.177 --> 01:05:10.857
He must have heard it from
Steve just before he got shot.

1006
01:05:10.937 --> 01:05:12.177
I found it on him.

1007
01:05:12.257 --> 01:05:14.297
Yes, ma, sure, we'll tell him.

1008
01:05:14.397 --> 01:05:15.857
That is, if I run across him.

1009
01:05:15.937 --> 01:05:17.457
No, I think it's...

1010
01:05:18.897 --> 01:05:22.097
Gosh, honey, I meant
to warn you about that.

1011
01:05:22.917 --> 01:05:24.137
Gee, well...

1012
01:05:25.177 --> 01:05:27.617
as much of me as she does or him.

1013
01:05:29.377 --> 01:05:31.397
Come on, Brass. Lift around the bunkhouse.

1014
01:05:31.477 --> 01:05:33.337
Maybe some of that licks us left.

1015
01:05:33.417 --> 01:05:35.777
Oh, come on. Come on, come here, you do.

1016
01:05:35.857 --> 01:05:37.197
What are you children doing?

1017
01:05:37.277 --> 01:05:39.317
You grew up playing rustler?

1018
01:05:39.397 --> 01:05:40.957
You said he would.

1019
01:05:41.457 --> 01:05:42.277
Sure.

1020
01:05:42.357 --> 01:05:45.797
That guy's a cattle
thief and more lanchine.

1021
01:05:46.117 --> 01:05:47.917
You children mustn't play like this.

1022
01:05:47.997 --> 01:05:49.938
You're liable to hurt each other.

1023
01:05:50.177 --> 01:05:52.397
Oh, he said he would.

1024
01:05:52.477 --> 01:05:54.677
He said he'd be seen.

1025
01:05:55.177 --> 01:05:56.177
Steve?

1026
01:05:56.257 --> 01:05:57.477
Sure.

1027
01:05:57.617 --> 01:06:01.077
Steve wasn't afraid
when they strung him up.

1028
01:06:01.157 --> 01:06:03.197
He didn't whimper at all.

1029
01:06:04.937 --> 01:06:06.877
Steve strung up?

1030
01:06:07.017 --> 01:06:08.237
Sure.

1031
01:06:08.337 --> 01:06:10.278
Well, what are you talking about?

1032
01:06:10.557 --> 01:06:13.797
Oh, Judge Henry Foreman
had to string him up.

1033
01:06:13.877 --> 01:06:16.297
Because they caught him stealing cattle.

1034
01:06:16.677 --> 01:06:19.137
You mean, hanged him?

1035
01:06:19.217 --> 01:06:20.257
Sure.

1036
01:06:40.977 --> 01:06:42.797
Happy birthday!

1037
01:06:55.617 --> 01:06:57.157
Is it true?

1038
01:06:58.377 --> 01:06:59.977
Is what true?

1039
01:07:00.317 --> 01:07:03.577
That Steve has been hanged.

1040
01:07:03.757 --> 01:07:05.857
Now, who's gone and told you that?

1041
01:07:05.937 --> 01:07:07.057
The children.

1042
01:07:07.277 --> 01:07:09.557
How on earth did them kids know?

1043
01:07:11.857 --> 01:07:13.377
Then it is true.

1044
01:07:14.037 --> 01:07:15.557
Well, you might as well know it.

1045
01:07:15.637 --> 01:07:18.137
Don't see why you wasn't
told in the first place.

1046
01:07:18.217 --> 01:07:21.570
Steve was strung up with the
rest of them cattle thieves.

1047
01:07:21.657 --> 01:07:22.657
Oh.

1048
01:07:26.317 --> 01:07:27.877
Did... did he do it?

1049
01:07:28.637 --> 01:07:29.997
Somebody had to do it.

1050
01:07:30.077 --> 01:07:32.397
He was in charge and it had to be done.

1051
01:07:33.017 --> 01:07:34.797
That's our kind of law.

1052
01:07:54.657 --> 01:07:57.037
Don't you realize that
was downright murder?

1053
01:07:57.117 --> 01:07:59.977
Now, there ain't no use
talking about it, dearie.

1054
01:08:00.057 --> 01:08:02.797
Crimes is ranked different
in different countries.

1055
01:08:02.877 --> 01:08:07.137
And out here, stealing's about the
meanest, the lowest thing a man can do.

1056
01:08:07.217 --> 01:08:09.297
But that doesn't justify killing.

1057
01:08:09.377 --> 01:08:11.197
and Steve is friends.

1058
01:08:11.277 --> 01:08:13.577
It ain't a question of friends or enemies.

1059
01:08:13.657 --> 01:08:15.717
It's a question of right and wrong.

1060
01:08:15.837 --> 01:08:18.997
Why, if we didn't hold a rope and
a six-shooter over them outlaws,

1061
01:08:19.077 --> 01:08:21.017
you couldn't teach your school at all.

1062
01:08:21.097 --> 01:08:23.497
Why, our lives wouldn't be worth nothing.

1063
01:08:23.577 --> 01:08:25.957
Do you think I'll teach my
children to believe in that?

1064
01:08:26.037 --> 01:08:29.397
Do you think I'll help raise the
new generation to approve of murder?

1065
01:08:29.477 --> 01:08:33.477
Well, where you come from, they have
policemen and courts and jails to enforce the

1066
01:08:33.557 --> 01:08:34.117
law.

1067
01:08:34.197 --> 01:08:39.137
Here, we got nothing. So when we
have to, we do things our own way.

1068
01:08:39.217 --> 01:08:42.629
Do you think it was easy for
him to have to hang a friend?

1069
01:08:42.737 --> 01:08:46.197
It was a darn sight harder for him
to do it than for us to bear it.

1070
01:08:46.277 --> 01:08:49.057
And there he is, just
because of lawlessness.

1071
01:08:49.137 --> 01:08:50.597
Somebody took a shot at him.

1072
01:08:50.677 --> 01:08:53.077
And you can't tell me it was Indian.

1073
01:08:53.977 --> 01:08:57.517
I suppose this country has
destroyed every human feeling in you.

1074
01:08:57.597 --> 01:08:58.977
And in him.

1075
01:08:59.397 --> 01:09:01.677
I suppose in time I'd feel that way too.

1076
01:09:01.757 --> 01:09:02.797
But I won't.

1077
01:09:02.877 --> 01:09:05.642
Then why don't you go
back where you come from?

1078
01:09:05.817 --> 01:09:06.997
I will.

1079
01:09:07.077 --> 01:09:08.377
As soon as he's well.

1080
01:09:08.457 --> 01:09:10.077
I won't stay in this place any longer.

1081
01:09:10.157 --> 01:09:10.977
All right.

1082
01:09:11.057 --> 01:09:12.237
Go on back home.

1083
01:09:12.317 --> 01:09:13.837
You don't belong here.

1084
01:09:13.917 --> 01:09:15.637
We don't want your kind.

1085
01:09:15.717 --> 01:09:17.097
Go on back east.

1086
01:09:17.177 --> 01:09:19.257
We're living soft and easy.

1087
01:09:19.357 --> 01:09:22.457
Sit on your silk cushions and
get hired girls to wait on you.

1088
01:09:22.537 --> 01:09:24.397
And drink your pink tea.

1089
01:09:26.497 --> 01:09:31.497
Why, when I married Taylor, I drove an ox
team a thousand miles from Council Bluffs

1090
01:09:31.577 --> 01:09:32.717
to this very spot.

1091
01:09:32.797 --> 01:09:38.497
I fought Indians with my father's rifle,
and him lying dead across my knees.

1092
01:09:38.637 --> 01:09:41.197
I killed a two-square with their own axe.

1093
01:09:41.277 --> 01:09:43.777
And you were talking.

1094
01:09:44.897 --> 01:09:48.837
This is a new country we're building up
here, and there ain't no room in it for

1095
01:09:48.917 --> 01:09:51.437
weaklings, men or women.

1096
01:09:51.857 --> 01:09:56.157
Go on back east, and I for
one will say good riddance.

1097
01:10:06.497 --> 01:10:08.197
Now you listen to me.

1098
01:10:08.857 --> 01:10:11.537
My people built a country
in New England, too.

1099
01:10:11.617 --> 01:10:15.097
And they fought and died just
as bravely as you Westerners.

1100
01:10:15.577 --> 01:10:18.597
Do you think you're the only
people who ever fought Indians?

1101
01:10:18.677 --> 01:10:21.501
Did you ever hear of the
Cherry Valley Massacre?

1102
01:10:21.837 --> 01:10:25.397
Well, my grandfather Stark was killed
in a blockhouse at Cherry Valley.

1103
01:10:25.477 --> 01:10:30.237
And my grandmother works 90 miles on
foot to get help to save the 14 survivors.

1104
01:10:30.317 --> 01:10:34.117
Don't tell me I can't do
anything when it's got to be done.

1105
01:10:34.277 --> 01:10:37.117
I can stand anything you can and more.

1106
01:10:39.137 --> 01:10:40.757
I'm not going away.

1107
01:10:41.357 --> 01:10:43.828
I'm going to stay here and look after him.

1108
01:10:47.977 --> 01:10:49.997
And now you get out of here.

1109
01:10:50.117 --> 01:10:51.157
Get out!

1110
01:10:51.237 --> 01:10:52.337
Get out!

1111
01:10:52.417 --> 01:10:54.197
You get out of here!

1112
01:11:08.137 --> 01:11:09.997
I warned you, Steve.

1113
01:11:10.377 --> 01:11:12.017
I warned you.

1114
01:11:12.397 --> 01:11:14.737
How could you have done this to me?

1115
01:11:17.877 --> 01:11:19.537
It's all right, darling.

1116
01:11:19.617 --> 01:11:21.037
It's all right.

1117
01:11:22.097 --> 01:11:24.177
I'm trying to understand.

1118
01:11:26.537 --> 01:11:28.537
Let's never talk about it.

1119
01:11:30.477 --> 01:11:32.837
Never let it come between us.

1120
01:11:33.537 --> 01:11:35.397
Forget it ever happened.

1121
01:11:38.137 --> 01:11:40.257
I can't help it, ma'am.

1122
01:11:41.157 --> 01:11:44.717
I think Romeo was a mangy on my...

1123
01:12:00.637 --> 01:12:04.637
It's a great mall, it's
a great man on the ground.

1124
01:12:04.717 --> 01:12:08.897
And another little drink
for the Joe's any heart.

1125
01:12:08.977 --> 01:12:11.177
Ah, shut up that rotten noise.

1126
01:12:11.257 --> 01:12:12.377
Come on, boys, let a drink.

1127
01:12:12.457 --> 01:12:13.837
Come on, Joe, set up another round.

1128
01:12:13.917 --> 01:12:15.137
What's the matter, you paralyzed?

1129
01:12:15.217 --> 01:12:17.377
What'd you ask? You know what I want.

1130
01:12:17.457 --> 01:12:19.157
Town's full of mean-gy cowboys.

1131
01:12:19.237 --> 01:12:20.857
What's up, hey, they?

1132
01:12:21.297 --> 01:12:22.077
Wedding.

1133
01:12:22.157 --> 01:12:25.677
Judge Henry Foreman's getting
married to the school board.

1134
01:12:25.757 --> 01:12:27.457
Oh, him, eh?

1135
01:12:27.537 --> 01:12:29.417
You think he would marry us?

1136
01:12:30.537 --> 01:12:35.337
I do seem to recollect something
about him being shot a while ago.

1137
01:12:36.097 --> 01:12:37.537
Injuns, wasn't it?

1138
01:12:37.797 --> 01:12:38.717
Yeah.

1139
01:12:38.797 --> 01:12:41.217
Somebody plugged him in the back.

1140
01:12:44.857 --> 01:12:46.377
Hello, sweetheart.

1141
01:12:46.457 --> 01:12:47.457
Come here.

1142
01:12:47.817 --> 01:12:51.597
The boy is the only woman in
Wyoming that's always on time.

1143
01:12:51.677 --> 01:12:53.737
Well, it's 8 o'clock, you know?

1144
01:12:53.817 --> 01:12:55.377
And here I am.

1145
01:12:57.137 --> 01:13:00.237
We're going to get some
chili and some flat jacks.

1146
01:13:00.317 --> 01:13:03.670
After that, we'll be back to
the bar for more punishment.

1147
01:13:06.577 --> 01:13:08.297
Come on, darling.

1148
01:13:12.437 --> 01:13:14.917
Hey, did you see who I saw?

1149
01:13:14.997 --> 01:13:17.137
Yeah, the mangy cow thief.

1150
01:13:17.317 --> 01:13:19.257
Looks like a lot of bad news to me.

1151
01:13:19.337 --> 01:13:21.217
Sure does. Hello, boys. Hello, Jim.

1152
01:13:21.297 --> 01:13:23.179
When's it going to be? Tomorrow?

1153
01:13:23.277 --> 01:13:25.997
Yeah, the bishop's making a
trip special just to marry him.

1154
01:13:26.077 --> 01:13:27.057
You don't say.

1155
01:13:27.137 --> 01:13:28.457
Ain't never seen a bishop.

1156
01:13:28.537 --> 01:13:29.737
What's the bishop look like?

1157
01:13:29.817 --> 01:13:31.877
Oh, just like an ordinary shoe drummer.

1158
01:13:31.957 --> 01:13:34.486
Except he wears half
his clothes backwards.

1159
01:13:35.597 --> 01:13:38.217
Howdy, Miss Wood. How do you do?

1160
01:13:38.297 --> 01:13:40.397
Won't be Miss Wood this time tomorrow.

1161
01:13:40.477 --> 01:13:41.117
No?

1162
01:13:41.197 --> 01:13:44.017
Good gracious, you do
look pretty in the picture.

1163
01:13:44.097 --> 01:13:47.237
Much prettier than that girl on
the Pride of Iowa kind of course.

1164
01:13:47.317 --> 01:13:49.577
Oh, thanks. Where's Ma and Dad Taylor?

1165
01:13:49.657 --> 01:13:50.597
Oh, they'll be along soon.

1166
01:13:50.677 --> 01:13:52.206
They came by Indian Creek.

1167
01:13:52.597 --> 01:13:54.597
I'll get everything ready,
and you come right on.

1168
01:13:54.677 --> 01:13:56.577
Howdy, Miss Molly. Oh, hello, boys.

1169
01:13:56.657 --> 01:13:57.897
Welcome to the bride.

1170
01:13:57.977 --> 01:13:59.837
We've been waiting all morning.

1171
01:13:59.917 --> 01:14:01.777
Well, I hardly expected you so soon.

1172
01:14:01.857 --> 01:14:03.257
They got something planned.

1173
01:14:03.337 --> 01:14:05.157
I can see it in their faces.

1174
01:14:05.237 --> 01:14:07.457
Howdy, boys. Howdy, boys.

1175
01:14:07.537 --> 01:14:09.297
He's from right, Miss Molly.

1176
01:14:09.377 --> 01:14:11.777
Could we borrow him for a spell?

1177
01:14:12.117 --> 01:14:15.457
Can I trust you? Oh,
we'll all be very good.

1178
01:14:15.537 --> 01:14:16.697
Pretty good.

1179
01:14:16.777 --> 01:14:18.437
Not too good.

1180
01:14:18.537 --> 01:14:20.197
Well, which is the honest man?

1181
01:14:20.277 --> 01:14:21.837
Not one of them.

1182
01:14:23.577 --> 01:14:25.237
Well, I'll trust all of you.

1183
01:14:25.317 --> 01:14:29.493
I'm going upstairs now, and you can
drink to his health all you please.

1184
01:14:31.617 --> 01:14:33.397
Sure thing. See you later.

1185
01:14:34.337 --> 01:14:35.717
We'll be waiting.

1186
01:14:38.417 --> 01:14:40.877
You don't mind my going
with him, do you, honey?

1187
01:14:40.957 --> 01:14:42.237
Of course not.

1188
01:14:42.317 --> 01:14:44.817
The boys have their rights
to you just as much as I have.

1189
01:14:44.897 --> 01:14:46.277
It won't be long.

1190
01:14:46.577 --> 01:14:48.871
Anyhow, the Taylors will be along soon.

1191
01:14:48.977 --> 01:14:51.918
We'll have plenty of time
alone where we're going.

1192
01:14:53.437 --> 01:14:54.937
We've traveled west.

1193
01:14:55.237 --> 01:14:57.897
We find just the place we want.

1194
01:14:57.977 --> 01:14:59.617
To make our home.

1195
01:15:00.217 --> 01:15:02.377
I hope you'll never be sorry.

1196
01:15:03.277 --> 01:15:05.957
I hope I'll always be
able to make you happy.

1197
01:15:06.757 --> 01:15:08.297
To keep you happy.

1198
01:15:08.537 --> 01:15:10.997
That's gonna be my main aim in life.

1199
01:15:15.317 --> 01:15:17.997
Now run along. The boys
are waiting for you.

1200
01:15:20.857 --> 01:15:24.151
The boys brought your thingies
and they're all upstairs.

1201
01:15:29.917 --> 01:15:32.297
Hello, boys. Hello, Branker.

1202
01:15:32.977 --> 01:15:34.817
Well, we set up about four of them.

1203
01:15:34.897 --> 01:15:35.897
Let's get to it.

1204
01:15:35.977 --> 01:15:37.777
Much obliged to you, boys.

1205
01:15:37.857 --> 01:15:40.197
I didn't know Francis was in town.

1206
01:15:40.437 --> 01:15:42.857
It looks like he's having more trouble.

1207
01:15:42.937 --> 01:15:46.408
He's been hanging around.
Talking plenty and drinking more.

1208
01:15:47.757 --> 01:15:49.037
Well, boys,

1209
01:15:49.377 --> 01:15:51.657
my last drink with you.

1210
01:15:52.977 --> 01:15:53.997
Single.

1211
01:15:54.317 --> 01:15:57.537
Here's how. Well,
fire and fall back, boys.

1212
01:15:57.737 --> 01:16:00.057
Some day, maybe I'll step off too.

1213
01:16:00.277 --> 01:16:01.377
Here's luck.

1214
01:16:02.057 --> 01:16:05.537
I'm glad you know there's
a friend of yours in town.

1215
01:16:06.537 --> 01:16:08.817
Did he mention he was a friend of mine?

1216
01:16:08.897 --> 01:16:11.037
He said plenty about you.

1217
01:16:11.117 --> 01:16:13.017
Well, forget it.

1218
01:16:13.097 --> 01:16:16.277
Sure, what I hear goes in
one ear and out the other.

1219
01:16:18.857 --> 01:16:22.197
What weather ain't it?
Hot or up on the way.

1220
01:16:23.837 --> 01:16:28.617
This friend of yours said he'd drop in
again, in case there's any interest to you.

1221
01:16:28.697 --> 01:16:30.017
Well, it ain't.

1222
01:16:30.857 --> 01:16:32.617
Let's have another drink.

1223
01:16:34.017 --> 01:16:39.057
Say, did you get what you was
hunting in the Tetons last fall?

1224
01:16:39.257 --> 01:16:40.257
Yeah.

1225
01:16:40.637 --> 01:16:43.157
The sheep was sick in the Tetons all year.

1226
01:16:43.317 --> 01:16:45.097
Trampas claims different.

1227
01:16:51.717 --> 01:16:53.937
I'll take this thing off
your hands if you want.

1228
01:16:54.017 --> 01:16:56.097
Save me the trouble. Just say the word.

1229
01:16:56.177 --> 01:16:57.677
Any or all of it. No.

1230
01:16:57.757 --> 01:16:58.897
Thanks, boys.

1231
01:16:59.417 --> 01:17:01.417
This is a matter between us, too.

1232
01:17:02.477 --> 01:17:04.857
I'm only hoping you don't drift around.

1233
01:17:05.017 --> 01:17:07.429
But a fellow don't get married every day.

1234
01:17:07.617 --> 01:17:08.777
That's just it.

1235
01:17:08.857 --> 01:17:10.537
You've got to think of her.

1236
01:17:11.237 --> 01:17:12.977
Who else am I thinking of?

1237
01:17:13.057 --> 01:17:17.257
Well, I'm acting mayor of this town,
and I'll put him in the Calibos

1238
01:17:18.357 --> 01:17:21.197
I smell like a junkie, boys.

1239
01:17:23.277 --> 01:17:26.237
Well, Joe's place is getting
pretty crummy all of a sudden,

1240
01:17:26.317 --> 01:17:28.729
eh? Come on, sit up around with the boys.

1241
01:17:29.197 --> 01:17:31.668
Poughhands are drinking their mangy wages.

1242
01:17:34.477 --> 01:17:38.077
Somebody left the door
open and the wind blew in.

1243
01:17:38.157 --> 01:17:39.497
Ah, come here, Travers.

1244
01:17:39.577 --> 01:17:41.297
Let's drink to the bride and groom.

1245
01:17:41.377 --> 01:17:44.137
Might as well get good
and liquor for the wedding.

1246
01:17:44.217 --> 01:17:47.923
Well, I heard the only way a man
can get shot in the back is...

1247
01:17:50.157 --> 01:17:51.557
Hey, you.

1248
01:17:51.877 --> 01:17:53.737
I'm a friend of Trampas.

1249
01:17:53.817 --> 01:17:54.817
Yeah?

1250
01:17:55.517 --> 01:17:56.737
That's right.

1251
01:17:56.937 --> 01:18:01.217
You know what Trampas claims about
that affair of yours down in the Tetons?

1252
01:18:01.297 --> 01:18:05.657
That you run from a wrestler
with your tail between your legs.

1253
01:18:08.937 --> 01:18:13.177
Hey, fellow, if you wasn't drinking,
you might wake up in the morning and find

1254
01:18:13.257 --> 01:18:15.437
yourself seriously dead.

1255
01:18:20.437 --> 01:18:22.897
Come on, Joe. Drink honey, boys.

1256
01:18:22.977 --> 01:18:28.777
Ah, turn your tail, you ornery hound,
and shove your nose into the ground,

1257
01:18:28.857 --> 01:18:35.377
for I'm an hombre Texas bound,
so early in the morning.

1258
01:18:37.097 --> 01:18:40.197
Oh, I'm sick of this lavergum.

1259
01:18:41.057 --> 01:18:42.557
I hear you.

1260
01:18:42.917 --> 01:18:46.097
You've been spending up talking about my
cattle deals and they're having a showdown

1261
01:18:46.177 --> 01:18:47.477
with you here and now.

1262
01:18:48.497 --> 01:18:49.197
Shut up.

1263
01:18:49.277 --> 01:18:50.517
You keep out of this.

1264
01:18:51.997 --> 01:18:53.477
You I'm talking to.

1265
01:18:54.877 --> 01:18:58.077
Trampus, I'm trying not to
have any trouble with you.

1266
01:18:58.157 --> 01:19:01.137
Just now. Yeah, you've been
dodging us for five years.

1267
01:19:01.217 --> 01:19:03.057
You've taken plenty of
trouble to keep out of my way.

1268
01:19:03.137 --> 01:19:05.957
But I got your corral now,
and I'm calling your hand.

1269
01:19:06.037 --> 01:19:06.737
All right.

1270
01:19:06.817 --> 01:19:09.957
What do you got? I got the belief
you're a lying white leopard scum.

1271
01:19:10.037 --> 01:19:11.997
This country ain't big
enough to hold the two of us.

1272
01:19:12.077 --> 01:19:14.842
I'm giving you the sun
down to get out of town.

1273
01:19:15.477 --> 01:19:19.217
It's too bad you had to say that, Trampus.

1274
01:19:19.757 --> 01:19:20.777
Get out.

1275
01:19:20.937 --> 01:19:23.937
Get out by sundown or
I'll shoot you on sight.

1276
01:19:36.537 --> 01:19:37.557
Boys,

1277
01:19:38.637 --> 01:19:40.225
you'll oblige me, isn't it?

1278
01:19:42.997 --> 01:19:47.417
We understand that it's something
that nobody else can do for you.

1279
01:19:47.517 --> 01:19:49.497
I knew you'd all see us that way.

1280
01:19:49.577 --> 01:19:52.497
We'll see that nobody interferes.

1281
01:19:52.577 --> 01:19:54.797
I never thought Trampus had the guts.

1282
01:19:54.937 --> 01:19:59.057
I don't want her to
know till it's all over.

1283
01:19:59.137 --> 01:20:00.837
We ain't saying nothing.

1284
01:20:00.917 --> 01:20:02.437
You wouldn't understand.

1285
01:20:02.677 --> 01:20:05.397
He was raised different.

1286
01:20:06.197 --> 01:20:07.877
So long, Joe. Bye, honey.

1287
01:20:07.957 --> 01:20:08.957
Bye, boys.

1288
01:20:16.637 --> 01:20:18.297
It won't be long to wait.

1289
01:20:18.377 --> 01:20:20.497
The sun will be down in
less than half an hour.

1290
01:20:20.577 --> 01:20:22.097
Well, he's forced it on you.

1291
01:20:22.177 --> 01:20:23.777
So hurry up and get it over with.

1292
01:20:23.857 --> 01:20:26.737
Yeah, we want to get some
fun out of this wedding, too.

1293
01:20:26.817 --> 01:20:28.157
You ain't worried none, are you?

1294
01:20:28.237 --> 01:20:32.677
What, us? Who, me? Why, of course
not, you on the old cock road.

1295
01:20:42.437 --> 01:20:43.837
Thank you.

1296
01:21:14.477 --> 01:21:17.177
There's been so frightful waiting for you.

1297
01:21:18.557 --> 01:21:20.777
Who had to tell you about it?

1298
01:21:20.937 --> 01:21:22.597
The woman downstairs.

1299
01:21:22.797 --> 01:21:24.917
I wanted to run out and find you.

1300
01:21:24.997 --> 01:21:26.417
But I didn't.

1301
01:21:26.497 --> 01:21:28.777
I waited quietly in my room.

1302
01:21:30.217 --> 01:21:32.537
I'm sorry you had to be worried.

1303
01:21:32.817 --> 01:21:34.277
It doesn't matter.

1304
01:21:35.017 --> 01:21:37.117
Nothing matters now
that you're back again.

1305
01:21:37.197 --> 01:21:38.677
And it's all over.

1306
01:21:39.497 --> 01:21:41.177
Let's don't think about it.

1307
01:21:42.057 --> 01:21:43.497
What will we do now?

1308
01:21:43.577 --> 01:21:44.837
What now?

1309
01:21:45.397 --> 01:21:46.397
Now?

1310
01:21:48.057 --> 01:21:49.377
Nothing now.

1311
01:21:56.437 --> 01:21:58.817
I know it's a heap worse for you.

1312
01:22:00.657 --> 01:22:03.037
I wish you didn't have to wait alone.

1313
01:22:04.077 --> 01:22:05.897
But it won't be for long.

1314
01:22:08.617 --> 01:22:10.177
Why, what do you mean?

1315
01:22:11.777 --> 01:22:13.437
I did my best.

1316
01:22:14.477 --> 01:22:17.359
Let him say things to me
no man ever said before.

1317
01:22:18.757 --> 01:22:23.617
If I hadn't been thinking hard of you,
I reckon I'd have killed him then.

1318
01:22:24.697 --> 01:22:26.717
I gave him a chance to quit.

1319
01:22:27.537 --> 01:22:30.077
But he'd gone too far before the others.

1320
01:22:32.497 --> 01:22:34.577
It'll have to go on now.

1321
01:22:58.797 --> 01:23:00.457
What are you going to do?

1322
01:23:04.357 --> 01:23:06.537
I'm not going to let him shoot me.

1323
01:23:09.357 --> 01:23:10.357
But...

1324
01:23:10.997 --> 01:23:13.417
We can go away. It's not too late.

1325
01:23:13.497 --> 01:23:15.203
You can go away and let's go.

1326
01:23:15.537 --> 01:23:17.357
I've got to stay.

1327
01:23:17.797 --> 01:23:19.317
No, no.

1328
01:23:19.957 --> 01:23:21.277
There's something else.

1329
01:23:21.357 --> 01:23:22.677
There must be.

1330
01:23:24.357 --> 01:23:26.057
Think what it means.

1331
01:23:26.137 --> 01:23:27.857
Killing in cold blood.

1332
01:23:27.937 --> 01:23:29.937
You don't think I want to do this?

1333
01:23:30.157 --> 01:23:32.457
I tried to forgive the other killing.

1334
01:23:32.537 --> 01:23:34.837
Those cattle thieves and thieves.

1335
01:23:34.937 --> 01:23:37.597
I forced myself to think of it as you did.

1336
01:23:37.757 --> 01:23:40.517
Of public duty, law and order.

1337
01:23:40.837 --> 01:23:43.697
But this, this isn't the same.

1338
01:23:43.777 --> 01:23:46.657
It's just a thing. I don't want
to satisfy a personal grudge.

1339
01:23:46.737 --> 01:23:52.457
If you came to think me a coward, I couldn't
look them square in the eye ever again.

1340
01:23:53.317 --> 01:23:54.817
Or you either.

1341
01:23:54.957 --> 01:23:56.897
But that's just pride.

1342
01:23:57.137 --> 01:23:58.902
I don't know what you call it.

1343
01:23:59.237 --> 01:24:02.177
But it's something in
the feelings of a man.

1344
01:24:02.417 --> 01:24:04.277
Down deep inside.

1345
01:24:04.877 --> 01:24:07.037
Something a man can't go back on.

1346
01:24:08.237 --> 01:24:12.766
If anybody happened to say I was a thief,
I couldn't let him go on saying it.

1347
01:24:12.897 --> 01:24:18.137
It wouldn't matter what other people thought,
but I'd have to know inside of me that

1348
01:24:18.217 --> 01:24:21.237
I thought enough for my
own honesty to fight for it.

1349
01:24:21.317 --> 01:24:23.697
Then, to be like this always,

1350
01:24:24.317 --> 01:24:26.057
when will that ever end?

1351
01:24:26.137 --> 01:24:30.977
They'll always be killing to do until
this country ain't a meeting place for men

1352
01:24:31.057 --> 01:24:32.637
like Trampus.

1353
01:24:34.417 --> 01:24:38.757
Then think about us, you
and me, our life together.

1354
01:24:39.077 --> 01:24:40.997
That's what I am thinking of.

1355
01:24:45.657 --> 01:24:48.257
Your life has always been your own.

1356
01:24:48.777 --> 01:24:50.437
But now it isn't.

1357
01:24:50.517 --> 01:24:52.357
You've given it to me.

1358
01:24:52.617 --> 01:24:54.277
Don't take it away.

1359
01:24:56.317 --> 01:25:02.437
When I think of tomorrow,
of you and me, and of...

1360
01:25:11.897 --> 01:25:16.597
If you do this, there'll be
no tomorrow for you and me.

1361
01:25:24.017 --> 01:25:26.277
Oh, no, no.

1362
01:25:26.557 --> 01:25:28.037
Oh, don't go.

1363
01:25:28.117 --> 01:25:29.417
Don't go.

1364
01:25:30.417 --> 01:25:32.697
Oh, my sake, please.

1365
01:25:33.057 --> 01:25:35.237
Oh, it's you, your life.

1366
01:25:35.317 --> 01:25:37.157
I can't let you.

1367
01:26:10.457 --> 01:26:12.357
Oh

1368
01:26:28.117 --> 01:26:29.277
Give me a room.

1369
01:26:31.257 --> 01:26:32.517
With you.

1370
01:26:50.837 --> 01:26:52.537
Calm down.

1371
01:27:06.017 --> 01:27:07.777
Thank you.

1372
01:27:40.037 --> 01:27:43.337
Thank you.

1373
01:28:04.557 --> 01:28:06.477
Here it comes up, Dick.

1374
01:28:20.237 --> 01:28:22.017
Oh, Mary!

1375
01:28:22.097 --> 01:28:23.097
Mary!

1376
01:28:43.237 --> 01:28:44.577
Hello, boss.

1377
01:28:46.577 --> 01:28:47.957
Hello, boys.

1378
01:28:54.777 --> 01:28:57.437
Well, I guess I'll go
down to the post office.

1379
01:28:57.517 --> 01:29:00.637
Why, you ain't finished
your last drink yet, Greasy.

1380
01:29:08.917 --> 01:29:10.797
Thank you.

1381
01:30:00.957 --> 01:30:03.117
He's dead as a cold mackerel.

1382
01:30:18.457 --> 01:30:20.617
I reckon he landed off.

1383
01:30:22.197 --> 01:30:24.337
Gene, come here, Gents.

1384
01:30:27.777 --> 01:30:30.557
It's all over. You can
come out now, Gents.

1385
01:30:39.777 --> 01:30:42.017
Thank heavens, it wasn't you.

1386
01:30:49.457 --> 01:30:52.277
I love you so much.

